WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:56.471
http://subscene.com/u/659433
Improved by: @Ivandrofly

2
00:00:56.473 --> 00:00:58.316
<font color="#808080">(INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING)</font>

3
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:47.374
<font color="#804040">MAN</font>: <i><font color="#808080">(ON RADIO)</font> ...with some lingering
clouds around Kodiak Island.</i>

4
00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:48.834
<i>Look for a chance of
overnight showers</i>

5
00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:51.112
<i>along the mountainous areas
of South Eastern Alaska.</i>

6
00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:54.865
<i>And now back to music on
KBWZ, Alaska listens.</i>

7
00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.050
<font color="#804040">RICKY</font>: Brad?

8
00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:58.635
Wait, you cut out. What?
<font color="#808080">(COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO)</font>

9
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.512
No, dude, my parents
went to Europe

10
00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:02.577
and they sent us to Alaska
to hang outwith my uncle.

11
00:02:03.206 --> 00:02:04.833
It's fine.

12
00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:08.220
Yeah, my uncle is
a paleontologist.

13
00:02:08.378 --> 00:02:12.679
He collects dinosaur bones. I guess
he's taking us to work with him.

14
00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:13.846
Brad?

15
00:02:15.344 --> 00:02:17.346
Brad? Brad, are you there?

16
00:02:18.055 --> 00:02:19.523
Great, no signal.

17
00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:20.815
Where are we going anyway?

18
00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:21.979
I'll give you a clue.

19
00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.108
I got it in here somewhere.

20
00:02:25.646 --> 00:02:27.319
Ah, there we go!

21
00:02:29.358 --> 00:02:31.031
Check it out.

22
00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.245
What is it?

23
00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:37.499
That, my friend, is the
tooth of a Gorgosaurus.

24
00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.081
- Cool!
- Isn't it?

25
00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:42.917
You know, it was almost as big
as a T-Rex, but way faster.

26
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.924
They roamed the Earth millions of
years ago and they got wiped out.

27
00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:49.257
Their only living descendants
are birds and blah, blah, blah.

28
00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:51.979
Oh, come on, man. You used to love
dinosaurs, you were an expert.

29
00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.259
This guy must have
been really scary.

30
00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.833
How do you think
he lost his tooth?

31
00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:25.713
- The Gorge?
- Yeah.

32
00:03:26.081 --> 00:03:30.587
I wonder if he was in, like, a huge
fight with a load of other dinosaurs.

33
00:03:30.794 --> 00:03:35.641
My friend, Natalie, she ran into a
flagpole at school and lost two teeth.

34
00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:37.551
There was blood everywhere.

35
00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:39.978
Yeah, a flagpole will do that.

36
00:03:40.178 --> 00:03:41.430
Let's go!

37
00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:45.021
You sure you don't
want to come?

38
00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.728
I'm not really into
digging up dead things.

39
00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:51.277
All right. Well, stay
close to the truck.

40
00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.818
If you change your mind
just follow the trail up.

41
00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:55.156
Got it.

42
00:03:55.318 --> 00:03:56.444
Okay, bud.

43
00:03:59.156 --> 00:04:00.829
<font color="#808080">(BIRDS CHIRPING)</font>

44
00:04:04.453 --> 00:04:05.796
<font color="#804040">MALE VOICE</font>: Psst!

45
00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.504
<font color="#808080">(BIRD CAWING)</font>

46
00:04:17.174 --> 00:04:18.551
<font color="#804040">MALE VOICE</font>: Psst! Psst!

47
00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.353
Hey, kid.

48
00:04:23.013 --> 00:04:24.936
Yeah, you. I'm talking to you.

49
00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:28.022
What's wrong? You never
heard a bird talk before?

50
00:04:28.518 --> 00:04:30.691
You think you're pretty
smart, don't you?

51
00:04:30.854 --> 00:04:32.334
It's all right. I'm
not offended about

52
00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:34.323
those things you said
about my ancestors.

53
00:04:34.858 --> 00:04:37.953
Totally cool with it. You
should see your ancestors.

54
00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:40.364
Three words: U-g-ly.

55
00:04:40.572 --> 00:04:41.789
<font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>

56
00:04:42.365 --> 00:04:45.039
But you know that every
fossil tells a story...

57
00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.038
and this tooth tells
a pretty good one.

58
00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:50.958
So go ahead and pick it up.
Come on, come on, pick it up.

59
00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:53.210
Pick it up, pick it up!

60
00:04:53.418 --> 00:04:56.480
Come on, it won't bite you.
Not anymore, at least.

61
00:04:56.505 --> 00:04:57.757
<font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>

62
00:04:58.256 --> 00:05:02.432
it will, however, open a
window into the ancient past.

63
00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.439
A vibrant world of
wonder and danger,

64
00:05:05.555 --> 00:05:07.774
when dinosaurs
roamed the earth...

65
00:05:07.933 --> 00:05:11.278
and birds looked a
little more like this.

66
00:05:11.603 --> 00:05:15.733
There, you see? Now we can begin.
<font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>

67
00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:20.195
And try to keep up, will you?!

68
00:05:22.072 --> 00:05:27.078
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>70 million years ago, in the late
Cretaceous period of planet Earth...</i>

69
00:05:27.244 --> 00:05:29.463
there <i>lived</i> a miraculous...

70
00:05:29.579 --> 00:05:31.752
<i>bird. That's me, Alex!</i>

71
00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:37.255
<font color="#804040">BOY</font>: <i>Alexornis, meaning
Alexander's Bird, insectivore.</i>

72
00:05:37.879 --> 00:05:39.552
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Note the
beautiful plumage...</i>

73
00:05:39.714 --> 00:05:42.593
<i>majestic wingspan, the
classically curved beak.</i>

74
00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:45.805
<i>Not to brag, but I am kind
of the whole package.</i>

75
00:05:46.221 --> 00:05:48.974
<i>Of course, if you're familiar
with the Cretaceous Period,</i>

76
00:05:49.099 --> 00:05:51.101
<i>you probably know all of this.</i>

77
00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.027
Hmm.

78
00:05:53.645 --> 00:05:54.897
Now watch closely.

79
00:05:55.063 --> 00:05:58.909
This is a delicate operation,
best left to the professionals.

80
00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:02.199
Ah, the enticing
smell of decay.

81
00:06:02.529 --> 00:06:05.499
Look at this tartar build-up.
Mmm!

82
00:06:08.743 --> 00:06:10.461
Hey, watch it!
<font color="#808080">(GROWLS)</font>

83
00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.043
I'm telling you, it's
hard out here for a bird!

84
00:06:14.749 --> 00:06:16.092
<i>But enough about me.</i>

85
00:06:16.251 --> 00:06:19.881
<i>The story you're about to see
concerns a friend of mine.</i>

86
00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:22.048
<i>I gotta say, it's a
pretty good one,</i>

87
00:06:22.173 --> 00:06:24.141
<i>filled with mystery
and adventure...</i>

88
00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:26.057
<i>hope and despair.</i>

89
00:06:26.553 --> 00:06:29.602
<i>Excuse me while I take a
personal moment. Gotcha!</i>

90
00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:33.952
<i>By the way, this isn't the guy I was
talking about. It's his mother.</i>

91
00:06:33.977 --> 00:06:35.479
<i>She is a Pachyrhinosaurus.</i>

92
00:06:35.937 --> 00:06:40.659
<font color="#804040">GIRL</font>: <i>Pachyrhinosaurus, meaning
thick-nosed lizard, herbivore.</i>

93
00:06:41.818 --> 00:06:45.664
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>But pay attention, because the
adventures of her son, Patchi...</i>

94
00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:48.245
<i>are the stuff of legend.</i>

95
00:06:51.161 --> 00:06:53.755
<i>Which has nothing to do with
that stuff right there.</i>

96
00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:56.042
Let me at it. Hey,
that's not fair!

97
00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:58.339
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>There he is!
That's Patchi.</i>

98
00:06:58.501 --> 00:06:59.627
Mm-mm, barf.

99
00:06:59.794 --> 00:07:01.888
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>The runt of
the litter, the guy</i>

100
00:07:02.005 --> 00:07:04.133
<i>at the bottom of
the pecking order.</i>

101
00:07:04.341 --> 00:07:06.093
- <font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Hey, Patchi!
- Can't talk now, Alex!

102
00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:07.852
Trying to work on my
survival instincts!

103
00:07:08.011 --> 00:07:09.487
Excuse me, Alpha
male coming through.

104
00:07:09.512 --> 00:07:11.355
Pardon, I'm just
gonna have a bite.

105
00:07:11.514 --> 00:07:12.515
Back off, Patchi.

106
00:07:12.682 --> 00:07:13.683
What about my fair share?

107
00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:15.477
Your fair share was delicious.

108
00:07:15.644 --> 00:07:17.996
That's my big brother, Scowler.
He's usually really cool.

109
00:07:18.021 --> 00:07:21.651
He just gets weird around puke.
Mm, there's some of it now.

110
00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:25.161
Sometimes you gotta
think outside the nest.

111
00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:27.831
So now I just gotta
get out of the nest.

112
00:07:32.994 --> 00:07:36.624
<font color="#804040">BOY</font>: <i>Troodon, meaning
wounding tooth, omnivore.</i>

113
00:07:38.708 --> 00:07:41.712
Alex might say I'm a runt, but
you gotta start somewhere.

114
00:07:41.962 --> 00:07:43.885
From zero to hero, baby.

115
00:07:44.047 --> 00:07:46.891
Whoa, whoa, whoa, hold on. I'm
the one telling the story!

116
00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.678
I have more credibility here.
It's my story, Alex.

117
00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:52.142
Yeah, but I have a more
neutral perspective.

118
00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:54.065
Wait a minute. Are you
really gonna eat that?

119
00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:56.522
You know it. Mom's
cooking, and still warm!

120
00:07:56.685 --> 00:07:58.687
- Uh-oh! Run away!
- Where you going?

121
00:07:58.853 --> 00:08:00.150
All right, more for me.

122
00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:02.273
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Seriously, there's a
big monster behind you!

123
00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:04.902
Sure, there's a big monster
behind you too! <font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>

124
00:08:05.193 --> 00:08:06.240
<font color="#808080">(SCREECHING)</font>

125
00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:08.659
<font color="#808080">(SCREAMING)</font>

126
00:08:10.573 --> 00:08:12.575
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: So much for your
survival instincts!

127
00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:13.743
Help!

128
00:08:15.245 --> 00:08:16.417
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

129
00:08:19.998 --> 00:08:21.518
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>Okay, so I
quickly learned that</i>

130
00:08:21.543 --> 00:08:23.591
<i>not everybody eats
puked-up leaves.</i>

131
00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.730
<i>There are things out
here called meat-eaters.</i>

132
00:08:25.755 --> 00:08:28.884
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Exactly, and you, my friend,
are made up almost entirely of meat.</i>

133
00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.444
Hey, put me down!
Lam not a chew toy!

134
00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:32.570
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

135
00:08:32.595 --> 00:08:34.097
<i>PATCHY. Good thing
my dad showed up.</i>

136
00:08:34.264 --> 00:08:37.228
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>That's Bulldust,
Patchi's 6, 000-pound papa.</i>

137
00:08:37.253 --> 00:08:38.493
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>Nobody
messes with him.</i>

138
00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:39.861
Hey, Dad, little help?

139
00:08:40.437 --> 00:08:42.485
Oh! Whoa! Whoa!

140
00:08:42.731 --> 00:08:45.109
Thank you!

141
00:08:46.401 --> 00:08:47.448
<font color="#808080">(GROANS)</font>

142
00:08:50.113 --> 00:08:51.548
<font color="#808080">(GROANS)</font>

143
00:08:51.573 --> 00:08:53.120
Medic!

144
00:08:53.283 --> 00:08:56.457
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>Classic Dad. He
was a man of few words.</i>

145
00:08:56.619 --> 00:08:58.972
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Actually, he was</i>
a <i>man of one word.</i>

146
00:08:58.997 --> 00:09:01.125
<font color="#808080">(ROARING LOUDLY)</font>

147
00:09:02.292 --> 00:09:03.293
<i>That one.</i>

148
00:09:04.878 --> 00:09:07.256
Huh? What is that?

149
00:09:07.422 --> 00:09:09.800
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>That, my friend,
is a hole in your head.</i>

150
00:09:09.966 --> 00:09:13.971
<i>But don't worry, one day that hole
will be filled with greatness.</i>

151
00:09:14.137 --> 00:09:16.139
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>Right! Plus you
can hardly see it.</i>

152
00:09:16.306 --> 00:09:18.400
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Especially if you don't
look at it. Besides...</i>

153
00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:19.958
<i>mistakes are natural
at a young age.</i>

154
00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.152
Look at that!

155
00:09:21.311 --> 00:09:23.985
Leaving the nest was
totally worth it!

156
00:09:24.147 --> 00:09:26.207
Hey, what's going on up there?
<font color="#808080">(FLATULENCE)</font>

157
00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:27.654
<font color="#808080">(EXCLAIMING)</font>

158
00:09:28.276 --> 00:09:29.961
What is this?

159
00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:33.081
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>That is the price
of leaving the nest.</i>

160
00:09:34.157 --> 00:09:36.580
Oh, who are you?
You're pretty cool.

161
00:09:36.743 --> 00:09:38.837
Come over here!
Where you going?

162
00:09:38.995 --> 00:09:40.463
Hey, don't be afraid.

163
00:09:40.622 --> 00:09:42.670
I'm not gonna eat
you or anything.

164
00:09:42.832 --> 00:09:44.017
He will.

165
00:09:44.042 --> 00:09:45.214
<font color="#808080">(GASPS)</font>

166
00:09:45.502 --> 00:09:46.879
<font color="#808080">(SNIFFING)</font>

167
00:09:49.172 --> 00:09:52.176
Hey, there. Name's Patchi.
Wanna be friends?

168
00:09:53.843 --> 00:09:55.390
Wait, wait! Wait up!

169
00:09:55.553 --> 00:09:57.197
I don't always
smell like this!

170
00:09:57.222 --> 00:09:58.849
I'm just covered in
poop at the moment!

171
00:10:00.016 --> 00:10:03.236
Aw, come on! Are we playing tag?
Is that what this is?

172
00:10:03.394 --> 00:10:05.192
Okay, I guess I'm
it then, right?

173
00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.040
<font color="#808080">(GROWLING)</font>

174
00:10:07.065 --> 00:10:08.237
Whoa.

175
00:10:09.317 --> 00:10:13.242
<font color="#804040">GIRL</font>: <i>Ankylosaur, meaning
fused lizard, herbivore.</i>

176
00:10:14.864 --> 00:10:17.242
This thing is huge!

177
00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:20.162
Which means I should probably
steer clear of his butt.

178
00:10:20.328 --> 00:10:22.706
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Good for you, Patchi.
You're learning.</i>

179
00:10:25.375 --> 00:10:26.376
<font color="#808080">(SNEEZES)</font>

180
00:10:44.894 --> 00:10:49.195
Wow! This is the most beautiful
place I've ever seen.

181
00:10:52.068 --> 00:10:54.787
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>It's</i> a <i>future oil field,
so don't get too attached.</i>

182
00:11:06.457 --> 00:11:09.131
Hey! Pick on someone
your own size!

183
00:11:09.419 --> 00:11:12.639
Uh, you know, I mean, if that's
a convenient option for you.

184
00:11:12.797 --> 00:11:15.141
Oop, there he goes.
You lost him.

185
00:11:15.675 --> 00:11:18.645
<font color="#804040">BOY</font>: <i>Hesperonychus, meaning
Western claw, carnivore.</i>

186
00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:21.602
No, I didn't mean me!

187
00:11:21.764 --> 00:11:23.766
Oh, you misunderstood!
I meant my brother!

188
00:11:23.933 --> 00:11:25.480
Yeah, he's bigger,
he's meatier.

189
00:11:25.602 --> 00:11:27.650
He's a lot slower! Oh,
he's so tender... Oh!

190
00:11:28.313 --> 00:11:32.113
Hey, Ma. Oh, I had it, but
thanks for showing up.

191
00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:38.577
<font color="#808080">(GROWLS)</font>

192
00:11:40.617 --> 00:11:42.619
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>And so, with a
little help from Mom...</i>

193
00:11:42.785 --> 00:11:46.164
<i>Patchi returned from his first
adventure a little bit wiser...</i>

194
00:11:46.331 --> 00:11:49.130
<i>and a whole lot smellier.</i>

195
00:11:49.667 --> 00:11:52.796
Hey. Guys. You are not gonna
believe what just happened to me.

196
00:11:52.962 --> 00:11:55.932
Oh, my gosh! Did you just
take a poop shower?!

197
00:11:56.132 --> 00:11:57.133
No.

198
00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.643
Maybe.

199
00:11:59.093 --> 00:12:00.185
Define poop shower.

200
00:12:00.345 --> 00:12:03.519
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>They were all jealous, Patchi,
'cause you'd been out in the world.</i>

201
00:12:03.681 --> 00:12:06.184
<i>You were on your way
to becoming a grownup.</i>

202
00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.830
♪ <i> One day I fell in love and</i> ♪

203
00:12:10.855 --> 00:12:14.167
♪ <i> You took all of my heart</i> ♪

204
00:12:14.192 --> 00:12:17.962
♪ <i> Twenty four hours, ♪
♪ blue sky, sun rays</i> ♪

205
00:12:17.987 --> 00:12:20.673
♪ <i> Where there used to be grey</i> ♪

206
00:12:20.698 --> 00:12:21.841
<i>I Used to be grey</i>

207
00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:26.167
♪ <i> Say goodbye to ♪
♪ yesterday Oh, oh</i> ♪

208
00:12:26.871 --> 00:12:30.000
♪ <i> What a difference ♪
♪ today made I</i> ♪

209
00:12:41.177 --> 00:12:43.475
Right, Dad, got it!
Knock down the tree

210
00:12:43.596 --> 00:12:46.349
and feast on the leafy
Greens up top! Mmm-mmm.

211
00:12:46.641 --> 00:12:49.394
Yeah, I also got it, Dad. I'm
just gonna square up here and...

212
00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:50.857
knock down the tree!

213
00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.193
I'll square up and
knock down the tree.

214
00:12:53.356 --> 00:12:56.075
Oh, I'm gonna just gonna grab...
He's stronger than he looks.

215
00:12:56.234 --> 00:12:57.406
Gonna feast on that leafy...

216
00:12:58.403 --> 00:13:00.405
- Okay.
- <font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Uh, Dad?

217
00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.033
Are we really from
the same litter?

218
00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.708
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Okay, what's so special
about dust? I don't get it.

219
00:13:11.874 --> 00:13:14.502
<i>You roll around on your back and
you make some grunting noises.</i>

220
00:13:14.669 --> 00:13:16.592
- <i>I mean, how is that a hobby?
- PATCHY. What?</i>

221
00:13:16.754 --> 00:13:18.131
Oh, man! You haven't
lived until

222
00:13:18.256 --> 00:13:19.817
you've taken a dirt bath.
It's the best.

223
00:13:19.841 --> 00:13:21.593
Here, let me get
in there, fellas.

224
00:13:21.759 --> 00:13:24.228
Yeah, oh, boy!

225
00:13:24.387 --> 00:13:26.389
It's so fun.
You gotta try... <font color="#808080">(YELLS)</font>

226
00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.727
Hey, hey, hey!
Watch the plumage!

227
00:13:30.852 --> 00:13:32.729
- How would you like it if I did this?
- Ow!

228
00:13:32.854 --> 00:13:34.606
- Hey, watch the nose!
- You watch it!

229
00:13:34.772 --> 00:13:36.194
- You watch it!
- No, you watch it!

230
00:13:38.943 --> 00:13:41.913
<font color="#804040">GIRL</font>: <i>Alphadon, meaning
first tooth, omnivore.</i>

231
00:13:46.242 --> 00:13:48.745
Patch! Pachito, come
on, wait for me!

232
00:13:49.287 --> 00:13:52.632
I'm sorry I went all pre-historic
on you back there, okay, buddy?

233
00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:53.916
It's okay, Alex.

234
00:13:54.083 --> 00:13:55.130
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: What's going on?

235
00:13:55.293 --> 00:13:58.092
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Major is challenging your
father for the role of leader!

236
00:13:58.254 --> 00:13:59.801
It's a time honored tradition.

237
00:13:59.922 --> 00:14:03.301
Oh, yeah, and Major's toast!
Dad's gonna crush him!

238
00:14:04.093 --> 00:14:06.095
Come on, Dad! Show
him who's boss!

239
00:14:06.262 --> 00:14:08.310
Introduce your
horn to his head!

240
00:14:08.473 --> 00:14:10.475
- Yeah, smack.
- Ah! Quit it!

241
00:14:10.641 --> 00:14:12.063
Hey. Dad!

242
00:14:12.226 --> 00:14:13.728
Wow, Dad, that was awesome!

243
00:14:13.895 --> 00:14:16.114
You kicked his butt all the
way up to the Stone age.

244
00:14:16.939 --> 00:14:18.082
Get back here!

245
00:14:18.107 --> 00:14:19.780
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>I may have been
smaller than my brother.</i>

246
00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:21.753
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>But you made up
for it by running</i> away.

247
00:14:21.778 --> 00:14:23.746
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>No, no, no. I
wasn't running away.</i>

248
00:14:23.863 --> 00:14:25.786
<i>I was racing him...
and winning.</i>

249
00:14:26.449 --> 00:14:27.746
- Are you ready?!
- Yeah.

250
00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.827
Are you sure? I'm pretty sure.

251
00:14:29.994 --> 00:14:31.962
Are you ready?! H it me!

252
00:14:32.288 --> 00:14:33.335
All right!

253
00:14:34.791 --> 00:14:36.134
- I wasn't ready.
- Yeah.

254
00:14:36.292 --> 00:14:37.794
- I'm ready now.
- Be quiet.

255
00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.188
Come back, you
coward, both of you!

256
00:14:40.213 --> 00:14:41.397
We're good.

257
00:14:41.422 --> 00:14:44.767
I want some more. You want some more!
Everybody wants more and more?

258
00:14:44.926 --> 00:14:47.054
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Did you guys see that?
Totally rang his bell.

259
00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:05.822
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>And so the
young Pachyrhinosaur</i>

260
00:15:05.988 --> 00:15:08.207
<i>frolicked and fritted
away his youth.</i>

261
00:15:08.408 --> 00:15:11.161
<i>Why? I dunno. The kid
likes to frolic.</i>

262
00:15:11.327 --> 00:15:14.046
<i>But all that was
about to change.</i>

263
00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:18.226
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>And it all started
the day I met... Juniper.</i>

264
00:15:18.251 --> 00:15:19.753
<font color="#808080">(FUNKY MUSIC PLAYING)</font>

265
00:15:21.003 --> 00:15:22.522
♪ <i> Oh, baby</i> ♪

266
00:15:22.547 --> 00:15:23.890
♪ <i> Give it up</i> ♪

267
00:15:25.133 --> 00:15:26.680
♪ <i> Ain't no use I</i> ♪

268
00:15:29.512 --> 00:15:31.230
Hi, I'm Patchi.
I'm made of meat.

269
00:15:31.347 --> 00:15:33.065
That's not what
I meant to say.

270
00:15:33.224 --> 00:15:34.567
I meant to say, "I'm Patchi."

271
00:15:34.684 --> 00:15:36.027
Whoa, is that a
hole in your head?

272
00:15:36.185 --> 00:15:39.109
Uh, no. I mean...
yeah, technically...

273
00:15:39.355 --> 00:15:40.698
I like it.

274
00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:45.036
Ah, young love, so beautiful,
so precious. Gotcha!

275
00:15:45.445 --> 00:15:49.291
Really, I've never seen anything
like that before. <font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

276
00:15:49.532 --> 00:15:51.034
- Really?
- There's my mom.

277
00:15:51.242 --> 00:15:52.710
I'm sorry, I have to go.

278
00:15:52.827 --> 00:15:54.204
Ah, but we just met!

279
00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:56.543
I'm not supposed to talk
to guys outside my herd.

280
00:15:56.706 --> 00:15:57.923
Stupid rules.

281
00:15:58.082 --> 00:16:00.301
I'm sorry. Goodbye.

282
00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:03.885
Wait, wait, don't go!
Just stay for one minute!

283
00:16:04.046 --> 00:16:05.389
Ah, no!

284
00:16:07.049 --> 00:16:08.767
Sniff me out later, okay?

285
00:16:09.135 --> 00:16:10.319
Oh.

286
00:16:10.344 --> 00:16:11.391
<font color="#808080">(WHOOPING)</font>

287
00:16:11.721 --> 00:16:13.598
Yeah! She likes me!

288
00:16:13.764 --> 00:16:15.937
And she likes my hole.

289
00:16:17.393 --> 00:16:20.897
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Over the next few days,
Patchi returned to the waterfall...</i>

290
00:16:21.063 --> 00:16:25.694
<i>for he had been bitten by the love
bug, the tastiest bug of all.</i>

291
00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:29.410
<i>But the lady proved
to be elusive.</i>

292
00:16:31.657 --> 00:16:33.580
<i>Not to be denied,
the young lover</i>

293
00:16:33.743 --> 00:16:35.666
<i>pursued his passion
nonetheless...</i>

294
00:16:35.828 --> 00:16:39.674
<i>once more returning to the
sight of his glorious vision.</i>

295
00:16:40.625 --> 00:16:43.128
<i>And he just kept
coming back...</i>

296
00:16:44.086 --> 00:16:46.760
<i>really to the point of overkill,
if you want my opinion.</i>

297
00:16:48.591 --> 00:16:50.514
Ah, man. Where is she?

298
00:16:51.302 --> 00:16:53.680
Oh, didn't I tell you?
She moved South.

299
00:16:53.846 --> 00:16:55.519
South? When?

300
00:16:55.681 --> 00:16:56.898
Four or five days ago.

301
00:16:57.058 --> 00:16:58.776
How long have you known this?

302
00:16:58.935 --> 00:17:00.937
About four or five days.
Gotcha!

303
00:17:01.938 --> 00:17:03.281
<font color="#808080">(SIGHS)</font>

304
00:17:06.567 --> 00:17:08.615
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>But Juniper and
her family were headed.</i>

305
00:17:08.736 --> 00:17:10.784
<i>South as part of the
great migration...</i>

306
00:17:10.947 --> 00:17:14.747
<i>for the summer was coming to an
end and food was in short supply.</i>

307
00:17:14.909 --> 00:17:19.665
<i>Especially the bug supply, which
is very, very important to me.</i>

308
00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:23.794
<i>More than anything, Patchi
wanted to follow Juniper...</i>

309
00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.930
<i>and his impatience was
beginning to show.</i>

310
00:17:27.088 --> 00:17:30.718
The birds are going South. Those
green things are going South.

311
00:17:30.883 --> 00:17:32.430
When do we get to go South?

312
00:17:32.593 --> 00:17:35.404
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: It'll be time to go when
your father says it's time.

313
00:17:35.429 --> 00:17:36.646
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

314
00:17:37.765 --> 00:17:38.812
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: It's time.

315
00:17:38.975 --> 00:17:40.192
Move 'em out, Patchi.

316
00:17:40.309 --> 00:17:41.561
You don't have to
tell me twice.

317
00:17:41.727 --> 00:17:43.570
Move 'em out, Patchi.

318
00:17:44.146 --> 00:17:47.025
Right, here we go.
My first migration.

319
00:17:56.617 --> 00:17:57.618
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

320
00:17:59.245 --> 00:18:00.963
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Eat my dust, Patchi.

321
00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:02.753
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: It's not a race.

322
00:18:03.499 --> 00:18:05.351
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Come on, guys,
don't be shy.

323
00:18:05.376 --> 00:18:07.378
We're all going to
the same place.

324
00:18:19.181 --> 00:18:22.105
Hey, Alex, don't most
birds fly South?

325
00:18:22.351 --> 00:18:26.697
It's called symbiosis, buddy. I get
transportation and you get pest control.

326
00:18:26.856 --> 00:18:27.857
Gotcha!

327
00:18:28.024 --> 00:18:30.447
Seriously, you're a
buffet on four legs.

328
00:18:31.027 --> 00:18:34.201
<i>And the herd lumbered South
across the Alaskan hinterland...</i>

329
00:18:34.363 --> 00:18:35.924
<font color="#804040">PATCH</font>: <i>Whoa, what do
you mean, lumbered?</i>

330
00:18:36.073 --> 00:18:37.842
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Well, you weren't
exactly gallivanting.</i>

331
00:18:37.867 --> 00:18:40.370
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>Yeah, we're Pachyrhinosaurs.
We don't gallivant.</i>

332
00:18:40.536 --> 00:18:42.538
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>No, you do not,
but I have to warn you,</i>

333
00:18:42.705 --> 00:18:44.582
<i>every good story
has a scary part</i>

334
00:18:44.707 --> 00:18:46.630
<i>and that's coming
up, so get ready.</i>

335
00:18:46.792 --> 00:18:48.886
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>Oh, I'm ready.
I lived through it.</i>

336
00:18:49.045 --> 00:18:51.889
<i>It was late afternoon and the
clouds were gathering in the east.</i>

337
00:18:52.048 --> 00:18:54.801
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Okay, okay, let me
tell it. I have the flair.</i>

338
00:18:54.967 --> 00:18:57.311
<i>The clouds gathered
in the east.</i>

339
00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.689
<i>Soon, a portent of
approaching danger</i>

340
00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:02.058
<i>floated in upon the
changing winds...</i>

341
00:19:02.224 --> 00:19:05.103
a <i>harbinger in the form of a
glorious winged creature.</i>

342
00:19:05.269 --> 00:19:07.738
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Danger, danger, everyone!
Warning, warning!

343
00:19:07.897 --> 00:19:09.615
Did you hear that, Dad?
Danger.

344
00:19:09.774 --> 00:19:12.072
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Of course he heard.
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

345
00:19:12.902 --> 00:19:14.779
What'd I say, huh?

346
00:19:15.821 --> 00:19:17.823
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>My father ordered
the herd into the Forest</i>

347
00:19:17.948 --> 00:19:20.009
<i>to find shelter
from the storm.</i>

348
00:19:20.034 --> 00:19:21.331
<font color="#808080">(THUNDER RUMBLING)</font>

349
00:19:31.921 --> 00:19:35.095
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>The weather worsened, and
my friend Patchi's young life...</i>

350
00:19:35.257 --> 00:19:37.430
<i>was about to change in a ﬂash.</i>

351
00:19:39.929 --> 00:19:41.947
I'm scared. <font color="#808080">(GASPS)</font>

352
00:19:41.972 --> 00:19:44.942
I'm not scared. You're the
only one who's scared.

353
00:19:45.101 --> 00:19:46.102
<font color="#808080">(SCREECHES)</font>

354
00:19:47.144 --> 00:19:50.068
Well, you and maybe that guy.
Wusses.

355
00:19:54.151 --> 00:19:57.906
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>The dry summer months had
turned the Forest into</i> a <i>tinderbox...</i>

356
00:19:58.072 --> 00:20:00.666
<i>ready to explode into flames.</i>

357
00:20:01.075 --> 00:20:03.624
<i>I know you humans like to
think you discovered fire...</i>

358
00:20:03.786 --> 00:20:05.504
<i>but trust me, it's been around</i>

359
00:20:05.621 --> 00:20:07.339
<i>since the time of
the dinosaurs.</i>

360
00:20:08.165 --> 00:20:10.543
<i>Patchi's father
smelled trouble.</i>

361
00:20:12.753 --> 00:20:14.881
<i>Quickly, he called to the others.
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font></i>

362
00:20:16.507 --> 00:20:19.056
<i>This was no time
to dilly-dally.</i>

363
00:20:19.218 --> 00:20:20.970
Dad, what's going on?

364
00:20:22.221 --> 00:20:24.189
- What is it, Alex'?
- It's fire!

365
00:20:24.348 --> 00:20:26.692
What's fire? Does
it eat meat?!

366
00:20:27.268 --> 00:20:29.191
It eats everything. Run!

367
00:20:29.353 --> 00:20:32.277
Go on! Move your
meaty little legs!

368
00:20:44.618 --> 00:20:47.622
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Bulldust and his family
hurried toward open ground.</i>

369
00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:52.293
<i>But there was
just one problem:</i>

370
00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:53.677
<i>Predators.</i>

371
00:20:54.044 --> 00:20:58.595
<i>For one dinosaur's misfortune
is another dinosaur's feast.</i>

372
00:20:59.258 --> 00:21:01.681
Hi there! Friend or foe?

373
00:21:02.428 --> 00:21:04.726
Foe, foe, definitely foe!

374
00:21:04.972 --> 00:21:06.724
Wait up, guys!

375
00:21:23.532 --> 00:21:26.411
Scowler, I don't like migration!
I wanna go home!

376
00:21:26.577 --> 00:21:29.000
Patchi, try and be
brave like Dad.

377
00:21:30.623 --> 00:21:32.296
What do we do now?
What do we do?!

378
00:21:32.458 --> 00:21:34.756
Don't worry, Dad would
never abandon me.

379
00:21:34.919 --> 00:21:36.045
You mean us, right?

380
00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:37.262
Right, us.

381
00:21:37.546 --> 00:21:38.843
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Help, Dad!

382
00:21:39.006 --> 00:21:40.633
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Dad, over here!

383
00:21:43.469 --> 00:21:44.509
That was a good idea, Dad.

384
00:21:44.637 --> 00:21:47.015
I was gonna do the same thing,
bust through that tree.

385
00:21:48.641 --> 00:21:50.018
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Hey, where's Mom?

386
00:21:56.482 --> 00:21:57.904
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Separated
from the others...</i>

387
00:21:58.067 --> 00:22:01.913
<i>Patchi's mom didn't realize that
she was heading into a trap.</i>

388
00:22:05.491 --> 00:22:06.743
<font color="#808080">(SNARLING)</font>

389
00:22:07.409 --> 00:22:09.753
<i>She did what she
could to protect her</i>

390
00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:12.248
<i>little ones, but the
danger only mounted.</i>

391
00:22:12.414 --> 00:22:16.715
<i>Severely outnumbered, she called
for Bulldust to come and help.</i>

392
00:22:17.253 --> 00:22:18.505
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

393
00:22:23.592 --> 00:22:24.809
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

394
00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:28.030
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: We should go with him.

395
00:22:28.055 --> 00:22:30.023
Patchi, Dad said to wait here!

396
00:22:30.182 --> 00:22:32.276
I don't care. Dad!

397
00:22:32.434 --> 00:22:34.937
Let me do it. I'm louder. Dad!

398
00:22:35.229 --> 00:22:37.231
Wait a minute, Scowler,
I think I see him!

399
00:22:37.439 --> 00:22:38.440
Dad!

400
00:22:38.774 --> 00:22:40.242
He's coming back!

401
00:22:40.401 --> 00:22:42.119
That's definitely... not him.

402
00:22:42.862 --> 00:22:44.580
Oh, boy, oh, boy,
run, run, run!

403
00:22:45.865 --> 00:22:48.288
We should split up. He'll
only eat one of us.

404
00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:49.451
The slower one, right?

405
00:22:49.618 --> 00:22:51.620
On second thought, we
better stick together!

406
00:22:51.787 --> 00:22:53.755
Over here, under those logs!

407
00:22:57.293 --> 00:23:00.797
I think we lost him. The smoke
is disguising our scent.

408
00:23:01.714 --> 00:23:03.808
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Really? You think?

409
00:23:07.303 --> 00:23:11.274
His tongue touched me! I was
literally on the tip of his tongue!

410
00:23:13.976 --> 00:23:15.148
Dad!

411
00:23:15.269 --> 00:23:16.429
I knew he'd come back for me!

412
00:23:16.604 --> 00:23:18.322
For us! You mean, us!

413
00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:20.448
Right, I said us.

414
00:23:20.816 --> 00:23:22.659
Get him, Dad! Stomp his butt!

415
00:23:22.818 --> 00:23:24.411
Yeah, get him, Dad!

416
00:23:24.904 --> 00:23:26.030
Do you think he'll win?

417
00:23:26.155 --> 00:23:27.327
What are you talking about?!

418
00:23:27.489 --> 00:23:29.992
Dad always wins.

419
00:23:30.159 --> 00:23:33.834
Always. Right? I
mean, he's got to.

420
00:23:36.081 --> 00:23:39.810
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>But this time, Bulldust,
the great Pachyrhinosaur...</i>

421
00:23:39.835 --> 00:23:43.430
<i>the most feared and
respected of his tribe...</i>

422
00:23:43.589 --> 00:23:45.512
<i>had met his match.</i>

423
00:23:45.674 --> 00:23:49.349
<i>On that day, noble
blood was spilled...</i>

424
00:23:49.678 --> 00:23:51.772
<i>while noble blood looked on.</i>

425
00:23:51.931 --> 00:23:53.478
It's gonna be okay.

426
00:23:53.682 --> 00:23:57.186
It's gonna be okay,
it's gonna be okay.

427
00:24:31.053 --> 00:24:32.726
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Anyone out there?

428
00:24:32.888 --> 00:24:34.310
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Can anyone hear us?

429
00:24:34.473 --> 00:24:35.690
Hello?

430
00:24:35.808 --> 00:24:37.025
Mom?

431
00:24:37.393 --> 00:24:38.565
Dad?

432
00:24:42.231 --> 00:24:44.154
Scowler, you see anything?

433
00:24:44.316 --> 00:24:46.569
Hello, anyone out there?

434
00:24:46.735 --> 00:24:48.578
Hello? Mom!

435
00:24:48.737 --> 00:24:50.831
- Patchi.
- Dad!

436
00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:53.163
Patchi, come on, we've
gotta keep moving.

437
00:24:53.325 --> 00:24:55.043
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: But what
if they come back?

438
00:24:55.202 --> 00:24:57.170
I don't know. They'll find us.

439
00:24:57.329 --> 00:24:59.081
Gotta get to the herd, okay?

440
00:24:59.248 --> 00:25:00.921
Yeah, but Scowler,
I'm just saying,

441
00:25:01.041 --> 00:25:02.759
what's the harm in
waiting a little?

442
00:25:02.918 --> 00:25:04.591
I'm sure they'd do
the same for us.

443
00:25:04.712 --> 00:25:06.430
They're not coming back, okay?

444
00:25:06.588 --> 00:25:08.590
Hello, Mom?

445
00:25:09.091 --> 00:25:12.345
I'm not giving up. Dad! Dad?!

446
00:25:13.595 --> 00:25:16.599
Aw, poor kid. I
wish I could help.

447
00:25:17.099 --> 00:25:19.022
Hey, somebody's coming!

448
00:25:19.184 --> 00:25:20.356
Dad?

449
00:25:20.894 --> 00:25:23.272
It's Major! Major!

450
00:25:24.023 --> 00:25:25.775
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Major, it's us!

451
00:25:25.941 --> 00:25:27.238
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Major!

452
00:25:27.693 --> 00:25:29.912
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Oh, Major, I'm
so happy to see you!

453
00:25:30.112 --> 00:25:31.534
It was crazy! There was
this fire, then these mean

454
00:25:31.655 --> 00:25:33.077
<i>psycho Gorges came
out of nowhere.</i>

455
00:25:33.240 --> 00:25:35.914
But Dad fought them off
and now he's gone...

456
00:25:36.076 --> 00:25:38.044
- Oh, okay.
- Geez.

457
00:25:38.287 --> 00:25:39.709
Good talk.

458
00:25:39.830 --> 00:25:41.457
Huh. He seemed kind of busy.

459
00:25:41.749 --> 00:25:43.968
I guess he's leader
of the herd now.

460
00:25:45.878 --> 00:25:47.380
Come on, follow me!

461
00:25:47.546 --> 00:25:49.940
Um, if he's the leader of the
herd, why am I following you?

462
00:25:49.965 --> 00:25:51.650
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: 'Cause I'm still
the leader of you! Come on!

463
00:25:51.675 --> 00:25:52.776
All right. I'm coming.

464
00:25:52.801 --> 00:25:55.145
We've got to stick together. It's
just you and me now, all right?

465
00:25:55.304 --> 00:25:57.056
Pay attention, and
watch your back.

466
00:25:57.222 --> 00:25:58.474
Yeah, I got it. Ooh!

467
00:25:58.724 --> 00:26:00.146
Sorry, ladies.

468
00:26:02.269 --> 00:26:05.489
Sweet pond scum, it's her!

469
00:26:05.647 --> 00:26:07.445
She looks amazing.

470
00:26:07.608 --> 00:26:10.487
Hey! Hey. Over here! Juniper!

471
00:26:10.652 --> 00:26:14.657
It's me! Uh, the guy with
the hole in his head?

472
00:26:14.823 --> 00:26:17.827
Hey, Patchi, you
migrating with us now?

473
00:26:17.993 --> 00:26:19.495
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: I've been looking
all over for you.

474
00:26:19.661 --> 00:26:21.163
I went back to the
waterfall so many times.

475
00:26:21.330 --> 00:26:23.958
But it was weird, it was
like you just disappear...

476
00:26:24.166 --> 00:26:26.009
Aw, come on!

477
00:26:27.169 --> 00:26:31.015
Oh, I see, playing hard to get.
Nice.

478
00:26:31.173 --> 00:26:32.675
I feel ya.

479
00:26:32.841 --> 00:26:35.685
Hey, Juniper, wait up!
Wait for me!

480
00:26:37.346 --> 00:26:39.314
What're you doing?
Who you talking to?

481
00:26:39.473 --> 00:26:41.191
Um, a friend.

482
00:26:42.351 --> 00:26:45.150
A friend? Since when
do you have friends?

483
00:26:45.604 --> 00:26:47.151
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: I have
tons of friends.

484
00:26:47.314 --> 00:26:51.035
Wait. Hold on! It's a girl, isn't it?!
<font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>

485
00:26:52.194 --> 00:26:53.241
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: What?

486
00:26:53.362 --> 00:26:54.454
Patchi's got a girlfriend.

487
00:26:54.613 --> 00:26:55.956
She's not my girlfriend.

488
00:26:56.073 --> 00:26:57.513
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: You might be
crushing a little.

489
00:26:57.616 --> 00:26:58.617
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Whose side
are you on, Alex?

490
00:26:58.742 --> 00:26:59.789
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: My side.

491
00:26:59.952 --> 00:27:02.546
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Admit it.
You're crushing hard.

492
00:27:02.704 --> 00:27:04.377
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Nope. Am not.

493
00:27:05.207 --> 00:27:07.301
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Give up! She's
out of your league!

494
00:27:08.377 --> 00:27:11.381
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>But Scowler's heckling was
not Patchi's only problem...</i>

495
00:27:11.964 --> 00:27:14.058
for the <i>north</i> wind had
started to blow...

496
00:27:14.216 --> 00:27:19.029
<i>revealing a musical side effect
to Patchi's perforated head.</i>

497
00:27:19.054 --> 00:27:20.556
<font color="#808080">(WIND WHISTLING)</font>

498
00:27:21.598 --> 00:27:23.692
What is that noise?

499
00:27:24.184 --> 00:27:26.437
Wait, is that me?

500
00:27:26.603 --> 00:27:28.071
Is my head whistling?

501
00:27:29.982 --> 00:27:31.325
Maybe nobody will notice.

502
00:27:31.733 --> 00:27:33.576
Whoa, what was that?

503
00:27:33.735 --> 00:27:36.454
Ave, ya-ya, please
turn that off.

504
00:27:38.073 --> 00:27:40.041
<font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>
Are you okay?

505
00:27:40.242 --> 00:27:43.462
Yeah, just whistling out
of my hole. No biggie.

506
00:27:43.620 --> 00:27:45.918
Told you you'd blow it.
Get it? Blow it.

507
00:27:46.081 --> 00:27:48.709
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Patchi, is that sound
really coming out of your head?

508
00:27:48.876 --> 00:27:49.877
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Uh, yeah it is.

509
00:27:50.043 --> 00:27:51.215
Well, I think it's cool.

510
00:27:51.378 --> 00:27:52.604
You're kidding, right?

511
00:27:52.629 --> 00:27:54.051
No, I'm not.

512
00:27:54.590 --> 00:27:57.139
Hey, I wish my frill
could whistle.

513
00:27:57.301 --> 00:27:59.679
Yeah, I wish my tail rattled.
We could do a duet.

514
00:27:59.845 --> 00:28:01.222
Ow, Scowler!

515
00:28:01.346 --> 00:28:02.707
Butt out, Scowler!
She's my friend.

516
00:28:02.848 --> 00:28:05.476
Shouldn't you ask her
mom for permission?

517
00:28:05.642 --> 00:28:07.485
I don't need to get
permission from her mom!

518
00:28:07.644 --> 00:28:08.645
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Patchi.

519
00:28:08.812 --> 00:28:11.656
Unless, of course, she is
standing right behind me.

520
00:28:11.815 --> 00:28:14.364
Which she is! What
a nice surprise!

521
00:28:14.568 --> 00:28:16.946
Hello, Mrs. Juniper's...
mom. Okay.

522
00:28:17.112 --> 00:28:19.114
- Bye, Patchi.
- Bye-bye, then.

523
00:28:19.281 --> 00:28:20.282
Good to see you.

524
00:28:20.449 --> 00:28:22.793
"Good to see you"? Seriously?

525
00:28:25.871 --> 00:28:28.044
Worst migration, ever.

526
00:28:28.707 --> 00:28:30.960
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>The winter rains
soon descended...</i>

527
00:28:31.126 --> 00:28:34.551
<i>casting</i> a <i>pall over the valley
and all who dwelled within.</i>

528
00:28:34.713 --> 00:28:38.934
<i>The continuous downpour soaked the
ground and dampened spirits...</i>

529
00:28:39.092 --> 00:28:42.392
<i>leaving many in a
very grumpy mood.</i>

530
00:28:51.647 --> 00:28:52.899
<font color="#808080">(SQUAWKS)</font>

531
00:28:59.279 --> 00:29:01.623
<i>We traveled days on end.</i>

532
00:29:01.823 --> 00:29:05.623
<i>Soon, days turned into weeks,
weeks turned into weekends...</i>

533
00:29:05.827 --> 00:29:07.921
<i>weekends turned
into long weekends.</i>

534
00:29:08.747 --> 00:29:10.670
<i>Well, you get the picture.</i>

535
00:29:11.083 --> 00:29:12.835
<i>By and by, there we were.</i>

536
00:29:13.001 --> 00:29:16.175
<i>Just a few short Miles from
the last mountain pass...</i>

537
00:29:16.338 --> 00:29:18.591
on <i>the way to the
winter grounds.</i>

538
00:29:19.174 --> 00:29:21.677
<i>Many creatures had made
the arduous journey...</i>

539
00:29:21.843 --> 00:29:24.437
not <i>only by land,
but on the wing...</i>

540
00:29:24.596 --> 00:29:27.941
<i>soaring high above the
pastoral terrain.</i>

541
00:29:29.309 --> 00:29:33.530
<font color="#804040">BOY</font>: <i>Pterosaur, meaning
winged lizard, carnivore.</i>

542
00:29:34.356 --> 00:29:37.860
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>While the poor earthbound
creatures plodded along...</i>

543
00:29:38.026 --> 00:29:41.656
<i>those of us blessed with certain
aerodynamic qualities...</i>

544
00:29:41.822 --> 00:29:43.870
<i>could cover hundreds of
Miles in a single...</i>

545
00:29:44.032 --> 00:29:46.677
Hey, watch it! I have
the right of way here!

546
00:29:46.702 --> 00:29:47.919
<font color="#808080">(SCREAMS)</font>

547
00:29:48.787 --> 00:29:50.130
You won't get away with this!

548
00:29:50.289 --> 00:29:51.640
You better watch your backs!

549
00:29:51.665 --> 00:29:54.714
I know some very
unsavory people.

550
00:29:55.002 --> 00:29:56.470
Sky hogs!

551
00:29:56.628 --> 00:30:00.804
<i>As I was saying, there it
was, the final mountain pass.</i>

552
00:30:00.966 --> 00:30:05.472
<i>Also known as the Widow-maker,
Dead Man's Canyon, Ambush Alley.</i>

553
00:30:05.637 --> 00:30:07.184
<i>It had a lot of names.</i>

554
00:30:07.347 --> 00:30:10.066
<i>Interesting sidebar for the
scientifically-minded.</i>

555
00:30:10.225 --> 00:30:12.899
<i>Did you know that the Pterosaur
has no natural predators?</i>

556
00:30:13.061 --> 00:30:14.404
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>Are you
sure about that?</i>

557
00:30:14.730 --> 00:30:17.153
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Yes, of course. I
don't make this stuff up.</i>

558
00:30:17.316 --> 00:30:18.909
<i>Fascinating
creatures, you know,</i>

559
00:30:19.026 --> 00:30:20.573
<i>light enough to
stay airborne...</i>

560
00:30:20.736 --> 00:30:24.582
<i>yet powerful enough to travel
great distances without rest.</i>

561
00:30:24.740 --> 00:30:26.492
<i><font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Really? And
no natural predators?</i>

562
00:30:26.616 --> 00:30:28.414
<i>"Alex". Nope. Not even one.</i>

563
00:30:28.535 --> 00:30:31.254
<i>The Pterosaur lives
a charmed life.</i>

564
00:30:31.580 --> 00:30:32.581
<i>Uh-oh.</i>

565
00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:37.586
<i><font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: I think you might have
just jinxed that guy, Alex.</i>

566
00:30:37.711 --> 00:30:40.590
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Sorry, boss, that's on me!
Keep it real, buddy!</i>

567
00:30:41.882 --> 00:30:43.930
<i>Did I mention that
the Pterosaur</i>

568
00:30:44.051 --> 00:30:46.099
<i>did have one natural
predator...</i>

569
00:30:46.261 --> 00:30:48.013
<i>the Gorgosaurus.</i>

570
00:30:48.555 --> 00:30:51.934
<font color="#804040">GIRL</font>: <i>Gorgosaurus, meaning
fierce lizard, carnivore.</i>

571
00:30:53.268 --> 00:30:57.614
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Nicely done. But I think</i> a
<i>little more is needed with this guy.</i>

572
00:30:58.774 --> 00:31:00.776
<i>Allow me to elaborate.</i>

573
00:31:02.194 --> 00:31:04.117
<i>Weighing in at nearly
two and a half tons...</i>

574
00:31:04.279 --> 00:31:05.872
<i>the Gorgosaur measured roughly</i>

575
00:31:05.989 --> 00:31:07.616
<i>26 feet from the
tip of his tail...</i>

576
00:31:07.783 --> 00:31:11.287
<i>to the top of his noggin, and if
you like teeth, he's got teeth.</i>

577
00:31:11.453 --> 00:31:13.547
<i>60 of them, and razor sharp.</i>

578
00:31:13.705 --> 00:31:17.084
<i>Perfect for tearing through
ﬂesh and splintering bones.</i>

579
00:31:17.250 --> 00:31:21.096
<i>His powerful legs propel him
to blazing speeds of up</i> to...

580
00:31:21.254 --> 00:31:23.598
<i>well, no one really knows, but he
certainly was faster than you.</i>

581
00:31:23.757 --> 00:31:25.680
<i>He was equipped
with an uncanny</i>

582
00:31:25.801 --> 00:31:27.803
<i>sense of smell, razor
sharp vision...</i>

583
00:31:27.969 --> 00:31:31.519
<i>and two tiny little arms.
He... <font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font></i>

584
00:31:32.265 --> 00:31:35.644
<i>I'm sorry. Seriously, I mean,
what's up with that? I mean...</i>

585
00:31:35.977 --> 00:31:38.981
<i>Okay, sorry, wait. I have
to compose myself. Okay.</i>

586
00:31:39.147 --> 00:31:42.572
<i>The Gorgosaurus had a
large brai...</i> <font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>

587
00:31:43.276 --> 00:31:44.823
<i>I'm sorry, I can't
take him seriously</i>

588
00:31:44.986 --> 00:31:46.488
<i>with those tiny
little baby hands.</i>

589
00:31:46.655 --> 00:31:50.080
<i>Look at him, he's so cute.
Okay, I'm sorry, sorry.</i>

590
00:31:50.242 --> 00:31:55.043
<i>But make no mistake, despite his
comically miniature arms... <font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font></i>

591
00:31:55.664 --> 00:31:57.132
<i>he was a very good eater...</i>

592
00:31:57.290 --> 00:32:01.420
<i>able to consume hundreds of pounds
of meat in a single feeding.</i>

593
00:32:09.344 --> 00:32:13.349
<i>I'll tell you what, you did not want
to get on a Gorgosaur's bad side.</i>

594
00:32:13.515 --> 00:32:17.941
<i>Oh, no, or on his insides, which
was a distinct possibility.</i>

595
00:32:18.103 --> 00:32:21.607
<i>Especially if you were a big
galumphing double-wide herbivore.</i>

596
00:32:24.443 --> 00:32:25.911
<font color="#808080">(SNIFFING)</font>

597
00:32:29.030 --> 00:32:31.533
<i>And featured on the menu
on this particular day...</i>

598
00:32:32.117 --> 00:32:36.346
<i>was Pachyrhinosaur Carpaccio
with a garnish of sagebrush...</i>

599
00:32:36.371 --> 00:32:39.796
<i>and just a soupcon
of wild asparagus.</i>

600
00:32:58.810 --> 00:33:02.735
Hey, Pachito! You feel like maybe
getting some exercise today?

601
00:33:02.898 --> 00:33:04.445
- What?
- Just got a strange feeling, that's all.

602
00:33:04.608 --> 00:33:06.235
You might wanna do a
little stretching,

603
00:33:06.401 --> 00:33:08.028
get those hamstrings
nice and loose.

604
00:33:08.195 --> 00:33:10.368
Just in case you decide
to do some cardio.

605
00:33:10.530 --> 00:33:13.409
Why would I be exercising
when I walk 12 hours a day?

606
00:33:13.575 --> 00:33:16.875
Because you might live longer!
Run away!

607
00:33:20.290 --> 00:33:24.045
Run away?! Away from what?! Where
do I go?! It'd be helpful to know!

608
00:33:36.264 --> 00:33:39.438
Keep to the center of the herd,
little bro! Safety in numbers!

609
00:33:39.601 --> 00:33:42.605
What's safe about this?!
I almost got stepped on!

610
00:33:42.771 --> 00:33:43.772
See?!

611
00:33:47.359 --> 00:33:48.611
<font color="#808080">(SNARLING)</font>

612
00:33:58.787 --> 00:34:02.792
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>The Gorgosaurs enacted their
plan with military precision.</i>

613
00:34:03.124 --> 00:34:05.627
<i>Now these bad boys of
the plains had it down.</i>

614
00:34:05.961 --> 00:34:08.931
<i>They chased and harried their
prey, causing panic...</i>

615
00:34:09.089 --> 00:34:10.807
<i>and introducing mayhem
in their ranks.</i>

616
00:34:10.966 --> 00:34:13.310
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: You'd freak out too if
they were chasing you, okay?

617
00:34:13.468 --> 00:34:15.095
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: I'm not judging.

618
00:34:16.304 --> 00:34:17.396
Juniper, this way!

619
00:34:17.556 --> 00:34:20.776
Mom, where are you?!
I'm going with Patchi!

620
00:34:23.144 --> 00:34:25.317
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Scowler, what are we
doing?! What's happening?!

621
00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:29.986
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Don't worry, <i>as</i> long <i>as</i> we
keep up with the herd, we'll be okay!

622
00:34:46.251 --> 00:34:48.629
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>And here, the nasty
Gorgosaurs separated</i>

623
00:34:48.753 --> 00:34:51.176
<i>the young and the
weak from the herd.</i>

624
00:34:54.175 --> 00:34:58.555
<i>Divide and conquer. Gorgon
practically invented it.</i>

625
00:35:03.226 --> 00:35:04.478
Patchi, what do we do?!

626
00:35:04.603 --> 00:35:05.855
Think happy thoughts!

627
00:35:13.320 --> 00:35:15.589
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Whatever happens,
we have to remain calm!

628
00:35:15.614 --> 00:35:16.957
Remember, they can smell fear!

629
00:35:18.074 --> 00:35:19.747
Sorry, that's not fear.

630
00:35:20.493 --> 00:35:21.745
Juniper, you okay?!

631
00:35:21.911 --> 00:35:23.538
I think I just stepped
in some fear!

632
00:35:30.920 --> 00:35:32.022
They have us cornered!

633
00:35:32.047 --> 00:35:33.594
Truce, truce! Time
out, time out!

634
00:35:36.134 --> 00:35:37.727
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Okay, everybody,
I got an idea.

635
00:35:37.886 --> 00:35:39.479
Just back up and
play it very cool.

636
00:35:39.638 --> 00:35:41.481
Like, we don't even
care, look at that

637
00:35:41.598 --> 00:35:43.441
nice stream over there,
let's look at...

638
00:35:44.601 --> 00:35:45.818
Somebody help me!

639
00:35:46.561 --> 00:35:48.563
Juniper! Oh, no!

640
00:35:48.897 --> 00:35:50.399
Swim towards the shore!

641
00:35:50.523 --> 00:35:52.025
I'm trying. I can't swim!

642
00:35:53.693 --> 00:35:55.036
PATCH I: <i>Juniper
needed my help.</i>

643
00:35:55.195 --> 00:35:57.038
<i>With her mom stuck
on the shore,</i>

644
00:35:57.155 --> 00:35:58.998
<i>I suddenly realized
what I had to do.</i>

645
00:35:59.157 --> 00:36:01.660
<i>I had to dive in to save her.
<font color="#808080">(GRUNTING)</font></i>

646
00:36:04.621 --> 00:36:05.713
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>You dove in?</i>

647
00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:06.922
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>That's right.</i>

648
00:36:07.082 --> 00:36:08.800
- <i>That was a dive?
- Yeah, actually.</i>

649
00:36:08.958 --> 00:36:10.710
- <i>It was.
- That was a dive, right there?</i>

650
00:36:10.877 --> 00:36:12.174
<i>Yeah, it was a dive.</i>

651
00:36:12.337 --> 00:36:14.385
<i>Maybe we should
look at that again.</i>

652
00:36:14.839 --> 00:36:15.840
<font color="#808080">(REWINDING)</font>

653
00:36:19.094 --> 00:36:20.311
<font color="#808080">(GRUNTING)</font>

654
00:36:20.845 --> 00:36:23.189
<i>Yeah, there you are
with a beautiful dive.</i>

655
00:36:23.636 --> 00:36:26.076
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>I'll have you know that
was a reverse pike cannonball.</i>

656
00:36:26.101 --> 00:36:28.695
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>I'll give you a 1.5
for degree of difficulty...</i>

657
00:36:28.853 --> 00:36:31.572
<i>and</i> a <i>perfect 10
for imagination.</i>

658
00:36:31.731 --> 00:36:34.109
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Help, I can't swim!

659
00:36:34.275 --> 00:36:38.997
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Hang in there, Patchi!
Whatever you do, try not to drown!

660
00:36:40.532 --> 00:36:45.459
<i>I watched my friend helplessly as he
was swept away into a watery grave.</i>

661
00:36:46.579 --> 00:36:47.580
PATCHI. <i>"Grave"?</i>

662
00:36:47.747 --> 00:36:48.919
<i>I'm still alive.</i>

663
00:36:49.082 --> 00:36:51.301
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Come on, it's</i>
a <i>figure of speech.</i>

664
00:36:55.171 --> 00:36:56.844
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Help, somebody!

665
00:36:57.424 --> 00:36:58.425
Help!

666
00:37:02.429 --> 00:37:03.601
Oh, thank goodness.

667
00:37:03.763 --> 00:37:05.356
Oh, that was a close one.

668
00:37:06.307 --> 00:37:08.275
Patchi! Over here!

669
00:37:08.435 --> 00:37:11.454
Hang on, Juniper! I'm
coming to save you!

670
00:37:11.479 --> 00:37:12.497
Yeah!

671
00:37:12.522 --> 00:37:14.708
Oh, man! That was close.

672
00:37:14.733 --> 00:37:16.376
I'm exhausted!

673
00:37:16.401 --> 00:37:17.544
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Whoa!

674
00:37:17.569 --> 00:37:18.570
Oh, my gosh!

675
00:37:19.891 --> 00:37:22.132
Whoa, that was scary! Oh, my
gosh, guys, can you help me?

676
00:37:22.157 --> 00:37:23.204
No! Whoa!

677
00:37:23.366 --> 00:37:25.869
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Thanks a lot, Scowler!
Nice work!

678
00:37:27.579 --> 00:37:29.502
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Patchi and the
others were carried</i> off...

679
00:37:29.664 --> 00:37:32.543
<i>by the swift and
treacherous current.</i>

680
00:37:38.882 --> 00:37:41.180
Patchi! Where are you?!

681
00:37:43.094 --> 00:37:44.266
Patchi!

682
00:37:44.429 --> 00:37:47.308
<i>I flew for what
seemed like days...</i>

683
00:37:47.474 --> 00:37:50.853
<i>but I do tend to exaggerate,
so, let's call it 10 minutes.</i>

684
00:37:51.227 --> 00:37:53.605
<i>Then, as I searched for
my dear friend Patchi...</i>

685
00:37:53.772 --> 00:37:56.992
<i>I was confronted by the specter
of his bloated corpse...</i>

686
00:37:57.150 --> 00:38:00.170
<i>cast upon the sand like
a lump of rotting ﬂesh.</i>

687
00:38:00.195 --> 00:38:01.504
- A mere shadow of a...
- Gotcha!

688
00:38:01.529 --> 00:38:02.746
Hey! What gives?

689
00:38:02.864 --> 00:38:04.081
See? I knew you were faking.

690
00:38:04.240 --> 00:38:06.117
That doesn't mean you
can poke my eye out!

691
00:38:06.284 --> 00:38:08.252
Agree to disagree, okay?
<font color="#808080">(SNEEZES)</font>

692
00:38:08.411 --> 00:38:09.628
Oh, gross!

693
00:38:09.788 --> 00:38:11.381
Mmm. But tasty.

694
00:38:11.539 --> 00:38:12.665
Charge!

695
00:38:12.832 --> 00:38:14.175
Hey, where's Scowler going?

696
00:38:14.334 --> 00:38:16.553
Come on, guys.
Here's the way out!

697
00:38:17.128 --> 00:38:18.801
Oh, wait. Hang on!

698
00:38:18.963 --> 00:38:21.557
Yeah, ocean. I'll
kick your salty butt.

699
00:38:21.716 --> 00:38:23.526
Yup, that's my brother.

700
00:38:23.551 --> 00:38:24.903
<font color="#808080">(JUNIPER GROANS)</font>

701
00:38:24.928 --> 00:38:26.145
Ouch.

702
00:38:26.304 --> 00:38:29.979
Come on, Juniper. Easy does it.
Ouch.

703
00:38:30.141 --> 00:38:31.939
Juniper! Are you okay?!

704
00:38:32.101 --> 00:38:33.728
Do not peck her eye out.

705
00:38:33.853 --> 00:38:35.446
Okay, relax!

706
00:38:35.605 --> 00:38:37.152
Are you all right? What's
wrong with your leg?

707
00:38:37.315 --> 00:38:39.409
Oh, it's just a scratch.

708
00:38:39.567 --> 00:38:42.741
Mostly I'm starving. I haven't
eaten since yesterday.

709
00:38:42.904 --> 00:38:44.156
Yeah, me neither.
<font color="#808080">(RUMBLING)</font>

710
00:38:44.364 --> 00:38:46.458
Whoa! Was that your stomach?

711
00:38:46.616 --> 00:38:48.493
Uh, definitely not.

712
00:38:48.660 --> 00:38:49.752
Look!

713
00:38:50.537 --> 00:38:51.914
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

714
00:38:57.877 --> 00:38:59.813
What is that?!

715
00:38:59.838 --> 00:39:01.481
<font color="#808080">(SCOWLER HUMMING)</font>

716
00:39:01.506 --> 00:39:03.133
Smack. What's that?

717
00:39:03.299 --> 00:39:05.267
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Ah, yes, the
mighty Edmontosaur...</i>

718
00:39:05.426 --> 00:39:08.771
<i>enormous in length,
gargantuan in height...</i>

719
00:39:08.930 --> 00:39:10.898
<i>and his brain? Not so much.</i>

720
00:39:11.057 --> 00:39:12.325
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>How big is your brain?</i>

721
00:39:12.350 --> 00:39:13.522
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>It's not</i> a <i>competition.</i>

722
00:39:14.269 --> 00:39:18.524
<font color="#804040">GIRL</font>: <i>Edmontosaurus, meaning
lizard of Edmonton, herbivore.</i>

723
00:39:22.610 --> 00:39:23.711
Whoa.

724
00:39:23.736 --> 00:39:25.079
- Heads up!
- Look out, Patchi!

725
00:39:25.238 --> 00:39:27.866
They look hungry. What
if they want to eat us?

726
00:39:28.032 --> 00:39:32.037
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: They don't eat meat,
they eat very large trees.

727
00:39:32.203 --> 00:39:33.500
I'm glad I'm not a tree.

728
00:39:33.621 --> 00:39:34.918
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Patchi. Come on!

729
00:39:35.081 --> 00:39:37.755
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>For once, luck had
smiled on our heroes...</i>

730
00:39:37.917 --> 00:39:40.170
<i>for within those
enormous animals'</i>

731
00:39:40.295 --> 00:39:42.548
<i>minuscule brains was
but one thought:</i>

732
00:39:42.714 --> 00:39:43.715
<i>Food.</i>

733
00:39:43.882 --> 00:39:45.108
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>What about a beverage?</i>

734
00:39:45.133 --> 00:39:47.761
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Okay, two thoughts, well,
three, if you want a side dish...</i>

735
00:39:47.927 --> 00:39:50.055
<i>but back to my original point.</i>

736
00:39:50.221 --> 00:39:52.565
<i>It was a most
fortuitous development,</i>

737
00:39:52.682 --> 00:39:55.026
<i>for as the ancient
wisdom tells us:</i>

738
00:39:55.184 --> 00:39:59.234
<i>If you want to know where the
food is, follow the fat guys.</i>

739
00:40:03.318 --> 00:40:04.478
You know what I was thinking?

740
00:40:04.485 --> 00:40:06.863
These guys are probably on their
way to some feeding ground.

741
00:40:07.030 --> 00:40:08.532
Maybe we should follow them.

742
00:40:08.698 --> 00:40:09.790
I just said that!

743
00:40:09.949 --> 00:40:11.301
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Good idea, Patchi.

744
00:40:11.326 --> 00:40:12.427
Thanks.

745
00:40:12.452 --> 00:40:14.204
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Oh, sure, Patchi,
take all the credit.

746
00:40:14.370 --> 00:40:16.372
Hey! Mind if we join you?

747
00:40:16.915 --> 00:40:18.633
You won't even
know we're here.

748
00:40:18.791 --> 00:40:22.546
In fact, I don't think you
do know we're here. Do you?

749
00:40:22.712 --> 00:40:23.713
No?

750
00:40:28.551 --> 00:40:30.178
Patchi, check it out!

751
00:40:30.803 --> 00:40:34.933
You go left, you go right, you gotta
be smarter than the herd... Ow!

752
00:40:37.936 --> 00:40:40.064
- Move it or lose it, lard butt.
- Ow. Scowler!

753
00:40:41.064 --> 00:40:42.782
Eat my dust.

754
00:40:42.982 --> 00:40:44.905
Again, not a race!

755
00:40:55.244 --> 00:40:57.963
Come on, June. We
gotta keep going.

756
00:40:58.206 --> 00:41:00.049
Hey. Juniper doesn't quit.

757
00:41:00.208 --> 00:41:03.758
I'm going as fast as three
and a half legs can take me.

758
00:41:22.563 --> 00:41:24.907
How's the leg, Juniper?
You need me to carry you?

759
00:41:25.274 --> 00:41:28.448
Nah, you know what? I'm just gonna
park it here for a bit. <font color="#808080">(SIGHS)</font>

760
00:41:28.736 --> 00:41:29.737
Oh, yeah.

761
00:41:29.904 --> 00:41:33.954
Oh, uh, having a lie-down, yeah.
Sure.

762
00:41:34.575 --> 00:41:36.828
Scowler! Wait up, Scowler!

763
00:41:40.248 --> 00:41:43.969
All right, so I guess we'll
catch up with you...

764
00:41:44.252 --> 00:41:45.799
or something, later?

765
00:41:46.254 --> 00:41:47.597
Guys? <font color="#808080">(SCOFFS)</font>

766
00:41:48.631 --> 00:41:50.508
Thanks for waiting!

767
00:41:51.259 --> 00:41:53.307
Save us some leafy Greens!

768
00:41:53.678 --> 00:41:55.976
Patchi, you should go on
ahead, I'll catch up.

769
00:41:56.139 --> 00:41:57.937
What are you, crazy? I'm
not going anywhere.

770
00:41:58.099 --> 00:42:00.602
I'm gonna stay with you
until you feel better.

771
00:42:09.110 --> 00:42:10.202
Patchi!

772
00:42:10.695 --> 00:42:12.789
Now where are those laggards?

773
00:42:12.947 --> 00:42:15.450
Ah, I should have guessed.

774
00:42:15.867 --> 00:42:19.121
Hey, I hate to horn in on
your beautiful moment...

775
00:42:19.287 --> 00:42:22.336
but in case you haven't
noticed, it's getting dark.

776
00:42:22.498 --> 00:42:24.876
Juniper, um, we
gotta get going.

777
00:42:25.877 --> 00:42:27.879
Okay, I'll be over here.

778
00:42:28.046 --> 00:42:30.720
I'm sorry to wake you,
but, I don't know...

779
00:42:30.882 --> 00:42:32.384
the tide turned or something.

780
00:42:32.508 --> 00:42:33.693
I don't really know
much about tides.

781
00:42:33.718 --> 00:42:35.812
But the point is, we need
to find another way out.

782
00:42:36.179 --> 00:42:37.647
Okay. Good luck with that.

783
00:42:37.805 --> 00:42:39.782
Okay, yeah, I can
get us out of here.

784
00:42:39.807 --> 00:42:42.026
Time to turn on my
trailblazing skills.

785
00:42:42.518 --> 00:42:44.987
Hey, Patchi, have you ever
had that weird dream...

786
00:42:45.146 --> 00:42:47.524
where a bunch of crabs are
crawling all over you?

787
00:42:47.690 --> 00:42:49.692
No. You know, I've had
the lobster dream but...

788
00:42:50.151 --> 00:42:52.074
Holy crab!

789
00:42:52.195 --> 00:42:53.196
Get them off!

790
00:42:53.488 --> 00:42:54.865
Here they come,
they're swarming

791
00:42:54.989 --> 00:42:56.841
and I don't know if
they're friendly! Ow!

792
00:42:56.866 --> 00:42:59.745
Hey, back off, shoo,
shoo, get out of here!

793
00:42:59.911 --> 00:43:02.710
Oh, I see you like to dance. So,
what will it be, my briny friend?

794
00:43:02.872 --> 00:43:04.670
The mambo?
<font color="#808080">(VOCALIZING)</font>

795
00:43:05.333 --> 00:43:08.382
The salsa? Perhaps
the deadly lambada?

796
00:43:08.544 --> 00:43:11.093
Tough guy, huh? Well, you've
messed with the wrong...

797
00:43:11.255 --> 00:43:12.982
Ow, ow! Get it off!

798
00:43:13.007 --> 00:43:17.433
<font color="#808080">(LAUGHS)</font> Look at them wiggle.
Wiggly-wiggly-woo.

799
00:43:17.678 --> 00:43:20.773
That's right, you run away!
You look so stupid!

800
00:43:20.932 --> 00:43:22.684
Oh, boy. Incoming!

801
00:43:22.892 --> 00:43:24.439
What does that mean?

802
00:43:24.602 --> 00:43:27.355
Hey, new friends, where are
you on the food chain?

803
00:43:27.522 --> 00:43:30.526
High, low, middle? Give
us a ballpark... Run!

804
00:43:33.027 --> 00:43:34.574
It's okay, they don't want us!

805
00:43:35.100 --> 00:43:36.380
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Then what
do they want?!

806
00:43:36.405 --> 00:43:37.406
The crabs!

807
00:43:37.573 --> 00:43:39.200
Ew, they just eat them whole?

808
00:43:39.367 --> 00:43:41.369
I guess they're purists.

809
00:43:41.536 --> 00:43:44.210
Come on Juniper, follow me! I'm
pretty sure it's this way.

810
00:43:44.372 --> 00:43:46.716
Lead on, Patchi, but
can we slow it down

811
00:43:46.833 --> 00:43:49.086
a Tad? Still a
little tender here.

812
00:43:49.252 --> 00:43:51.380
Oh, yeah, of course,
no problem.

813
00:43:53.339 --> 00:43:56.263
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>You see, Patchi was
already becoming a leader.</i>

814
00:43:56.425 --> 00:43:59.395
<i>A leader of one, but you
gotta start somewhere.</i>

815
00:44:03.349 --> 00:44:06.728
<i>The sun set for the last time
on the Western horizon...</i>

816
00:44:06.894 --> 00:44:09.067
<i>giving way to sister moon...</i>

817
00:44:09.230 --> 00:44:13.235
<i>who would now hold sway over the
wintery Alaskan wilderness...</i>

818
00:44:13.401 --> 00:44:16.780
<i>piercing the darkness
with her pale blue eyes.</i>

819
00:44:16.946 --> 00:44:18.789
<i>Which simply means,
it'll be dark</i>

820
00:44:18.906 --> 00:44:20.749
<i>in the Arctic for
a very longtime.</i>

821
00:44:21.909 --> 00:44:24.128
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <font color="#808080">(SHIVERS)</font> Yikes!
It's getting kinda chilly.

822
00:44:24.620 --> 00:44:25.872
We should have brought layers.

823
00:44:25.985 --> 00:44:28.266
Are you sure this is the right
way to the feeding grounds?

824
00:44:28.291 --> 00:44:31.761
Of course I'm sure. I got a knack
for these kinds of things.

825
00:44:31.919 --> 00:44:35.924
Besides, I've also got a foolproof
Plan B and his name is Alex.

826
00:44:36.257 --> 00:44:39.136
I hope there's a Plan C,
'cause I'm totally lost.

827
00:44:39.302 --> 00:44:42.772
Did you hear that? We're
lost in this horrible place.

828
00:44:42.930 --> 00:44:47.811
It's just a normal Forest full
of normal foresty things.

829
00:44:50.396 --> 00:44:51.397
What was that?

830
00:44:55.985 --> 00:44:57.282
<font color="#808080">(SCREECHING)</font>
<font color="#808080">(SCREAMS)</font>

831
00:44:58.946 --> 00:45:00.289
That's not funny!

832
00:45:00.740 --> 00:45:02.788
Take it somewhere
else, furball!

833
00:45:05.077 --> 00:45:07.330
You know, someday these
mammals will go extinct...

834
00:45:07.622 --> 00:45:10.341
and then we'll have the
last laugh. Ha ha!

835
00:45:17.632 --> 00:45:20.306
You know, it isn't actually
that bad out here.

836
00:45:20.468 --> 00:45:22.015
Think about it: A
dark creepy Forest

837
00:45:22.136 --> 00:45:23.683
is really just an open field...

838
00:45:23.846 --> 00:45:25.447
with trees and different
things in it.

839
00:45:25.598 --> 00:45:26.866
You never know what
you're gonna find.

840
00:45:26.891 --> 00:45:28.484
Oops. Watch the log.

841
00:45:29.018 --> 00:45:30.861
Uh, not log, tail.

842
00:45:31.020 --> 00:45:33.148
I hope it's not connected
to this claw in any way.

843
00:45:33.314 --> 00:45:36.363
Or that big toothy muzzle.

844
00:45:37.693 --> 00:45:40.162
Oh, I can't bear to watch...

845
00:45:40.321 --> 00:45:41.322
but I will.

846
00:45:41.989 --> 00:45:44.959
Careful, Patchi, don't
make any sudden movements.

847
00:45:45.117 --> 00:45:48.166
It's another kind of movement
I'm worried about right now.

848
00:45:48.829 --> 00:45:49.830
Okay.

849
00:45:49.956 --> 00:45:53.460
♪ <i> Nice little Gorgo ♪
♪ on the treetop</i> ♪

850
00:45:53.626 --> 00:45:57.347
♪ <i> While I climb over ♪
♪ Please don't wake-up I</i> ♪

851
00:45:57.505 --> 00:46:00.149
Now, I suggest you
slowly and gently...

852
00:46:00.174 --> 00:46:01.551
<font color="#808080">(SCREAMS)</font>
Run away, run away!

853
00:46:01.968 --> 00:46:04.028
What are you doing? Are you
trying to get us eaten?

854
00:46:04.053 --> 00:46:05.414
No, I'm not trying
to get us eaten.

855
00:46:05.429 --> 00:46:06.781
I'm trying to get
us out of here.

856
00:46:06.806 --> 00:46:10.856
Anyway, he's probably hibernating.
He won't wake-up till spring.

857
00:46:11.852 --> 00:46:14.196
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Maybe we should be a
bit more careful from now on.

858
00:46:14.689 --> 00:46:18.535
Yeah. From now on, I'm gonna be
extra careful and keep it stealthy.

859
00:46:18.693 --> 00:46:19.990
I'm gonna be like a ninja.

860
00:46:20.152 --> 00:46:23.247
There are probably plenty of other
things to worry about in these woods.

861
00:46:23.531 --> 00:46:24.532
Totally.

862
00:46:24.699 --> 00:46:28.203
Like, what other kind of
things you think are out here?

863
00:46:28.619 --> 00:46:32.874
<font color="#804040">GIRL</font>: <i>Chirostenotes, meaning
narrow-handed omnivore.</i>

864
00:46:33.207 --> 00:46:37.061
- Oh, Don't worry. This is kinda nice, right?
- Mmm-hmm.

865
00:46:37.086 --> 00:46:39.384
Little moonlit stroll.
Sort of like a date.

866
00:46:39.547 --> 00:46:41.857
Well, not like a date.
More like a hangout.

867
00:46:41.882 --> 00:46:44.527
Like a friendly
hang-sesh at night.

868
00:46:44.552 --> 00:46:46.020
<font color="#808080">(BOTH GASP)</font>
<font color="#808080">(SCREECHING)</font>

869
00:46:46.512 --> 00:46:47.559
Chirostenotes!

870
00:46:47.680 --> 00:46:48.727
Chiroste-nachos?!

871
00:46:48.889 --> 00:46:49.936
- Notes!
- Whaties?!

872
00:46:50.099 --> 00:46:53.729
Hey, beat it! Note-ies.
Chirostenotes. Enunciate!

873
00:46:54.013 --> 00:46:55.413
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: What kind
of a name is that?

874
00:46:55.438 --> 00:46:57.065
A long one. Get away!

875
00:46:57.231 --> 00:46:58.824
They give them crazy
names, I would have

876
00:46:58.941 --> 00:47:00.568
called them skinny-neck
pecky thingies.

877
00:47:00.735 --> 00:47:03.409
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: That's longer.
Maybe we should just focus.

878
00:47:03.571 --> 00:47:05.949
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: A little hard to focus
when they keep pecking!

879
00:47:06.115 --> 00:47:07.241
Patchi, they don't
have any teeth!

880
00:47:07.408 --> 00:47:08.785
But I do!

881
00:47:09.076 --> 00:47:10.077
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Yeah!

882
00:47:10.244 --> 00:47:11.724
- Got them good!
- Yeah! That's right!

883
00:47:11.746 --> 00:47:13.589
Who wants to get bit? You?!

884
00:47:13.706 --> 00:47:15.549
Back off, you skinny-neck
pecky thing!

885
00:47:15.708 --> 00:47:17.069
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Their
feathers taste gross.

886
00:47:17.209 --> 00:47:18.756
Take a hike, Turkey bird!

887
00:47:19.086 --> 00:47:20.759
Keep it movin'.

888
00:47:20.963 --> 00:47:24.092
What are you looking at?
Better move on!

889
00:47:24.258 --> 00:47:27.069
Yeah, that's what I thought!
<font color="#808080">(SCREECHING)</font>

890
00:47:27.094 --> 00:47:28.937
And so should we!
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

891
00:47:45.571 --> 00:47:46.572
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Wow!

892
00:47:47.615 --> 00:47:49.834
Oh, good, you're
seeing that, too?

893
00:47:49.992 --> 00:47:53.166
Just 'cause I thought it was
that rancid pinecone I ate.

894
00:47:54.330 --> 00:47:56.003
It's so beautiful.

895
00:47:57.333 --> 00:48:01.312
♪ <i> Oh, there's a river ♪
♪ that runs on forever</i> ♪

896
00:48:01.337 --> 00:48:04.181
♪ <i> I'm gonna see where it leads</i> ♪

897
00:48:05.257 --> 00:48:09.278
♪ <i> Oh, there's a mountain ♪
♪ that no man has mounted</i> ♪

898
00:48:09.303 --> 00:48:11.977
♪ <i> I'm gonna stand on the peak</i> ♪

899
00:48:13.140 --> 00:48:17.203
♪ <i> Out there's a land ♪
♪ that time don't command</i> ♪

900
00:48:17.228 --> 00:48:20.107
♪ <i> Wanna be the first to arrive</i> ♪

901
00:48:21.107 --> 00:48:25.127
♪ <i> No time for pondering ♪
♪ why I'm-a wandering</i> ♪

902
00:48:25.152 --> 00:48:27.996
♪ <i> On while we're ♪
♪ both still alive</i> ♪

903
00:48:28.739 --> 00:48:33.370
♪ <i> To the ends of the ♪
♪ earth, would you follow me</i> ♪

904
00:48:35.788 --> 00:48:40.464
♪ <i> There's a world that was ♪
♪ meant for our eyes to see</i> ♪

905
00:48:42.837 --> 00:48:45.090
♪ <i> To the ends of the earth...</i> ♪

906
00:48:46.173 --> 00:48:49.177
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: There they are! You
did it! You found them!

907
00:48:49.927 --> 00:48:51.725
We found them.

908
00:48:52.012 --> 00:48:53.264
<font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>

909
00:48:54.014 --> 00:48:56.108
Come on! Race you
to the bottom!

910
00:48:56.267 --> 00:48:57.894
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: That's my herd!

911
00:49:02.523 --> 00:49:03.775
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <font color="#808080">(LAUGHS)</font>
Slippery!

912
00:49:04.650 --> 00:49:06.823
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Look out below! Whoa!

913
00:49:07.361 --> 00:49:08.613
Wait up!

914
00:49:09.780 --> 00:49:12.299
Somebody got a second wind.
<font color="#808080">(LAUGHS)</font>

915
00:49:12.324 --> 00:49:13.426
Let's go!

916
00:49:13.451 --> 00:49:15.874
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Yeah! Full moon, cool!

917
00:49:16.036 --> 00:49:18.038
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Mom, Dad! We made it!

918
00:49:18.205 --> 00:49:20.207
Hey, everybody, it's us!

919
00:49:20.374 --> 00:49:22.468
- We're back!
- <font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Incoming!

920
00:49:22.626 --> 00:49:24.270
Hi, Garry. Looking
good, Phyl...

921
00:49:24.295 --> 00:49:27.094
Whoa, Phyllis, watch the tail.

922
00:49:27.465 --> 00:49:30.139
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Well, well, well, look
who's trotting into camp.

923
00:49:30.384 --> 00:49:33.558
Scowler, back after heroically
abandoning his brother.

924
00:49:33.804 --> 00:49:35.806
Greetings, my fickle friend.

925
00:49:36.640 --> 00:49:38.734
Uh, Alex, bite me.

926
00:49:40.561 --> 00:49:42.905
Mm, don't mind if I do.
<font color="#808080">(MUNCHING)</font>

927
00:49:45.733 --> 00:49:47.076
Hey! Hey, hey!

928
00:49:47.234 --> 00:49:49.657
Hey, Stretch, get
your own slimy rock.

929
00:49:49.820 --> 00:49:50.821
Yeah.

930
00:49:52.281 --> 00:49:56.787
♪ <i> To the ends of the ♪
♪ earth, would you follow me</i> ♪

931
00:49:59.205 --> 00:50:03.802
♪ <i> There's a world that was ♪
♪ meant for our eyes to see</i> ♪

932
00:50:06.086 --> 00:50:10.136
♪ <i> To the ends of the ♪
♪ earth, would you follow me</i> ♪

933
00:50:13.177 --> 00:50:17.683
♪ <i> If you won't, I must say ♪
♪ my goodbyes to thee I</i> ♪

934
00:50:32.780 --> 00:50:37.456
All right, little swimmy
thingies, I gotcha!

935
00:50:37.618 --> 00:50:39.620
- Aw, man!
- What are you doing?

936
00:50:39.954 --> 00:50:41.597
They've gotta come
up for air sometime.

937
00:50:41.622 --> 00:50:43.624
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Hey, losers!
<font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font>

938
00:50:43.958 --> 00:50:47.132
They looked. Where you
losers been, huh, Patchi?!

939
00:50:47.294 --> 00:50:49.137
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: What?! You
left us behind.

940
00:50:49.296 --> 00:50:51.344
- You left me ahead.
- That's ridiculous!

941
00:50:51.507 --> 00:50:52.608
You're ridiculous!

942
00:50:52.633 --> 00:50:54.635
No, you are ridiculous.

943
00:50:54.885 --> 00:50:57.388
Uh-uh, you're ridiculous!
You're ridiculous! <font color="#808080">(ICE CRACKS)</font>

944
00:50:57.638 --> 00:50:59.311
Oh, so cold!

945
00:51:02.309 --> 00:51:04.653
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Eventually the
sky, once shrouded</i>

946
00:51:04.770 --> 00:51:07.068
<i>in darkness for
months on end...</i>

947
00:51:07.231 --> 00:51:10.326
<i>was brightened by the
arrival of the sun.</i>

948
00:51:14.238 --> 00:51:15.706
<font color="#808080">(SQUAWKING)</font>

949
00:51:19.493 --> 00:51:20.494
<font color="#808080">(SQUAWKS)</font>

950
00:51:25.124 --> 00:51:27.218
<font color="#808080">(SHRIEKING)</font>

951
00:51:27.459 --> 00:51:30.008
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>The Alphadon came out of
his hole and saw his shadow...</i>

952
00:51:30.170 --> 00:51:32.298
<i>and you know what that
means: Winter was over.</i>

953
00:51:32.464 --> 00:51:34.637
<i>PATCHY. I thought winter was over
if he doesn't see his shadow.</i>

954
00:51:34.800 --> 00:51:37.519
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>You know absolutely
nothing about Alphadon Day.</i>

955
00:51:37.678 --> 00:51:39.180
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>It was around
that time that I noticed</i>

956
00:51:39.305 --> 00:51:40.807
<i>everybody was going
South again...</i>

957
00:51:40.973 --> 00:51:42.850
<i>but this time in reverse.</i>

958
00:51:43.017 --> 00:51:45.019
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>So North,
in other words.</i>

959
00:51:45.352 --> 00:51:46.353
<i>PATCHY. Exactly.</i>

960
00:51:46.520 --> 00:51:49.832
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Fortunately, Major was
there to give the word.</i>

961
00:51:49.857 --> 00:51:51.074
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

962
00:51:51.358 --> 00:51:53.736
<i><font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Am I wrong, or was that the
same as the word for going South?</i>

963
00:51:53.861 --> 00:51:55.909
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>It's a very
simple language.</i>

964
00:51:56.071 --> 00:51:58.494
<i>As he began the return
journey to his birthplace...</i>

965
00:51:58.657 --> 00:52:00.534
<i>Patchi reflected on the joys</i>

966
00:52:00.701 --> 00:52:02.578
<i>and heartaches of his
first migration.</i>

967
00:52:02.745 --> 00:52:05.514
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Come on, Patchi.
Northward ho!

968
00:52:05.539 --> 00:52:06.640
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Yeah.

969
00:52:06.665 --> 00:52:08.338
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Let's get to the
front, I'm tired of looking

970
00:52:08.459 --> 00:52:10.132
at people's butts
all the time.

971
00:52:10.294 --> 00:52:13.673
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Marching to a meter set
down by the change of seasons...</i>

972
00:52:13.839 --> 00:52:17.810
<i>Patchi's herd traveled the
same route year after year.</i>

973
00:52:18.052 --> 00:52:20.054
<i>They journeyed South...</i>

974
00:52:20.554 --> 00:52:22.022
<i>then North...</i>

975
00:52:22.181 --> 00:52:23.728
<i>then South again.</i>

976
00:52:23.932 --> 00:52:26.651
<i>I mean, seriously, what's wrong
with West once in a while?</i>

977
00:52:26.810 --> 00:52:30.064
<i>Or East, even, just to
spice things up, you know?</i>

978
00:52:30.314 --> 00:52:32.567
<i>Through it all, his
load was lightened</i>

979
00:52:32.733 --> 00:52:34.986
<i>by the splendid bird that
always had his back.</i>

980
00:52:35.152 --> 00:52:37.371
<i>Patchi and I collected
a lot of memories</i>

981
00:52:37.488 --> 00:52:39.707
<i>on those trips, and
even more bugs.</i>

982
00:52:39.865 --> 00:52:42.217
Gotcha! I'm stuck. I'm stuck.

983
00:52:42.242 --> 00:52:43.368
<font color="#808080">(GRUNTS)</font>

984
00:52:44.620 --> 00:52:46.088
Don't worry about me.
I'm fine.

985
00:52:46.246 --> 00:52:49.090
No, I love you too. Thanks a lot.
Yeah, I appreciate it, buddy.

986
00:52:52.419 --> 00:52:55.468
<i>But with each passing year
and every migration...</i>

987
00:52:55.631 --> 00:52:57.929
<i>Patchi grew bigger and bigger</i>

988
00:52:58.050 --> 00:53:00.348
<i>and his hole grew
larger and larger.</i>

989
00:53:00.511 --> 00:53:03.572
Hey, I told you one day his hole
would be filled with greatness.

990
00:53:03.597 --> 00:53:05.349
And here I am!

991
00:53:06.975 --> 00:53:10.354
<i>Yes, my little friend Patchi
was not so little anymore.</i>

992
00:53:11.188 --> 00:53:12.861
<i>He had grown into
a young adult...</i>

993
00:53:13.649 --> 00:53:15.526
<i>just in time for the
annual courtship...</i>

994
00:53:15.693 --> 00:53:19.618
<i>when mature males vie for the
affections of the females.</i>

995
00:53:20.781 --> 00:53:22.624
You know something, Patchi?

996
00:53:23.617 --> 00:53:26.370
I love the quality time we
spend together, really.

997
00:53:26.537 --> 00:53:30.337
But isn't it time you declared
your intentions with Juniper?

998
00:53:30.499 --> 00:53:32.219
'Cause headbutting season
has already begun.

999
00:53:32.376 --> 00:53:34.629
<font color="#808080">(SCOFFS)</font>
I hate headbutting season.

1000
00:53:34.753 --> 00:53:36.972
It's like all the adults
suddenly lose their minds.

1001
00:53:37.131 --> 00:53:40.135
With all the yelling and the
snorting and the circling...

1002
00:53:40.300 --> 00:53:41.301
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Don't forget
the headbutting.

1003
00:53:41.468 --> 00:53:44.972
Yeah, and the headbutting.
It's so... prehistoric.

1004
00:53:45.139 --> 00:53:46.857
But it is how things are done.

1005
00:53:47.015 --> 00:53:49.313
What? What kind of things?

1006
00:53:49.476 --> 00:53:52.730
I cannot interfere with matters of
the heart, it is against my policy!

1007
00:53:52.896 --> 00:53:54.318
Patchi loves you.

1008
00:53:54.481 --> 00:53:55.573
Huh?

1009
00:53:56.567 --> 00:53:59.867
Patchi! I was afraid you
weren't going to show up.

1010
00:54:00.028 --> 00:54:02.497
What? Of course I was.

1011
00:54:02.656 --> 00:54:05.000
And, wait, what am I showing
up for again? <font color="#808080">(LAUGHS)</font>

1012
00:54:05.159 --> 00:54:07.036
The headbutting
contest, silly.

1013
00:54:07.161 --> 00:54:09.038
Major is taking on
all challengers.

1014
00:54:09.204 --> 00:54:12.378
Who would be dumb enough to
challenge that guy? He's huge.

1015
00:54:12.499 --> 00:54:13.809
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

1016
00:54:13.834 --> 00:54:15.381
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: And it looks
like you're up.

1017
00:54:15.627 --> 00:54:16.719
What?!

1018
00:54:20.340 --> 00:54:24.140
I should sit this one out, 'cause I
just ate two huge Berry bushes and...

1019
00:54:24.303 --> 00:54:26.351
Step aside, Patchi.

1020
00:54:29.516 --> 00:54:30.768
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1021
00:54:34.521 --> 00:54:39.243
Hey, Major, it's time you went head
to head with a real Pachyrhinosaur!

1022
00:54:47.242 --> 00:54:49.244
I'll tell you what: Scowler
does not back down.

1023
00:54:49.411 --> 00:54:51.880
What's the big deal?
I could do that!

1024
00:54:52.581 --> 00:54:54.925
I've got 50 bugs
on the big guy.

1025
00:55:05.052 --> 00:55:07.851
If you're just going to chit
chat, I'm going to get a snack.

1026
00:55:08.013 --> 00:55:09.060
Hold my place.

1027
00:55:11.892 --> 00:55:15.442
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Ah, yes, the clash
of the Pachyrhinosaurs.</i>

1028
00:55:16.730 --> 00:55:19.734
<i>One of the great spectacles
of prehistoric pugilism.</i> ..

1029
00:55:19.900 --> 00:55:22.323
<i>Combining the Grace of ballet</i>

1030
00:55:22.444 --> 00:55:24.867
<i>with the stupidity of
banging into things.</i>

1031
00:55:25.239 --> 00:55:28.288
<i>This was to be a very
momentous contest...</i>

1032
00:55:28.450 --> 00:55:30.544
<i>for it was on that day...</i>

1033
00:55:30.702 --> 00:55:33.080
<i>that Scowler not
only took on Major,</i>

1034
00:55:33.205 --> 00:55:35.583
<i>the big boss of the
Pachyrhinosaurs...</i>

1035
00:55:36.250 --> 00:55:37.547
<i>but he defeated him.</i>

1036
00:55:42.214 --> 00:55:45.317
<i>And just like that,
a new Era was born.</i>

1037
00:55:45.342 --> 00:55:46.810
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

1038
00:55:47.553 --> 00:55:50.397
<i>Scowler was the new
leader of the herd.</i>

1039
00:55:53.267 --> 00:55:55.816
- Yeah!
- Way to go, Scowler! Nice.

1040
00:55:58.063 --> 00:56:01.067
Good fight, Major. Too
bad someone had to lose.

1041
00:56:01.275 --> 00:56:02.492
That was you, by the way.

1042
00:56:02.651 --> 00:56:04.449
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Man, that was epic.

1043
00:56:04.945 --> 00:56:05.946
Great job, buddy.

1044
00:56:06.113 --> 00:56:08.787
I'm not your buddy, I'm the
leader of the herd now.

1045
00:56:08.949 --> 00:56:10.326
Show some respect.

1046
00:56:10.492 --> 00:56:11.835
- But-but...
- Patchi!

1047
00:56:12.077 --> 00:56:13.624
How was I supposed to know?

1048
00:56:13.787 --> 00:56:15.222
Juniper where are you going?

1049
00:56:15.247 --> 00:56:17.591
Sorry, Patchi, it's
those stupid rules.

1050
00:56:17.749 --> 00:56:21.424
Law of the arctic, little bro.
You snooze, you lose.

1051
00:56:21.587 --> 00:56:23.339
But I didn't... I mean...

1052
00:56:23.505 --> 00:56:27.009
Hold on. How about a do-over?
Huh? Best of three?

1053
00:56:27.175 --> 00:56:28.597
I'm ready now, let's do it!

1054
00:56:28.760 --> 00:56:30.637
We're not kids anymore!

1055
00:56:30.804 --> 00:56:33.478
Come on, Juniper. Move out!

1056
00:56:33.682 --> 00:56:35.650
Oh, and Patchi...

1057
00:56:36.268 --> 00:56:40.444
I know, I know, eat your dust.

1058
00:56:51.658 --> 00:56:56.505
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>And the herd marched on, but this
time with Scowler leading the way.</i>

1059
00:56:56.663 --> 00:56:59.166
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Okay, this
is Scowler's herd...

1060
00:56:59.333 --> 00:57:02.132
and things are gonna be different
around here from now on!

1061
00:57:02.294 --> 00:57:04.396
Rule number one,
all herd members

1062
00:57:04.421 --> 00:57:07.174
will walk a minimum four
feet behind Scowler!

1063
00:57:09.009 --> 00:57:13.856
Rule number two, do not speak to
Scowler without first being spoken to.

1064
00:57:14.890 --> 00:57:19.191
Rule number three, do not make
direct eye contact with Scowler.

1065
00:57:19.686 --> 00:57:22.235
Rule number four, never
question or contradict Scowler.

1066
00:57:22.397 --> 00:57:24.365
The first Thursday
of every month

1067
00:57:24.524 --> 00:57:26.526
will be known as Scowler
Appreciation Day.

1068
00:57:26.693 --> 00:57:28.912
Suggested gifts include,
but are not limited to...

1069
00:57:29.071 --> 00:57:31.915
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>As if Patchi's bruised
ego wasn't bad enough...</i>

1070
00:57:32.074 --> 00:57:36.045
<i>now he had a big old heap of
heartbreak to go with it.</i>

1071
00:57:38.997 --> 00:57:41.045
Hey! Hey, get out,
you lousy squatter.

1072
00:57:41.208 --> 00:57:44.178
Cheer up, Patchi, it's not
the end of the world.

1073
00:57:44.336 --> 00:57:45.979
That won't come for
another couple years.

1074
00:57:46.004 --> 00:57:47.347
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Leave me
alone, would you?

1075
00:57:47.506 --> 00:57:49.554
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: You wanna talk about it?
You wanna share?

1076
00:57:49.716 --> 00:57:51.093
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Get off!

1077
00:57:51.259 --> 00:57:53.933
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: Okay, you're the boss!
Besides Scowler.

1078
00:57:54.096 --> 00:57:56.064
Too soon? Too soon, sorry.

1079
00:57:57.516 --> 00:58:00.895
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>The ice and snow had started
to thaw, but Patchi's heart?</i>

1080
00:58:01.061 --> 00:58:04.110
<i>Well, that was another matter.</i>

1081
00:58:04.564 --> 00:58:07.693
<i>Yep, these were tough times
for our lumbering hero.</i>

1082
00:58:07.901 --> 00:58:12.372
<i>But as the saying goes, when life
gives you lemons, make lemonade.</i>

1083
00:58:12.531 --> 00:58:14.341
<i>And when life puts
your brother in charge</i>

1084
00:58:14.366 --> 00:58:16.744
<i>and takes away the
girl of your dreams...</i>

1085
00:58:17.577 --> 00:58:19.170
<i>Well, that's-that's
a tough one.</i>

1086
00:58:19.287 --> 00:58:20.834
<i>Let me get back
to you on that.</i>

1087
00:58:38.390 --> 00:58:43.112
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Way to go, Scowler. Frozen
water, always fun to walk on.

1088
00:58:44.229 --> 00:58:46.527
I wish Juniper would
look back at me,

1089
00:58:46.648 --> 00:58:48.946
just give me some
sort of sign.

1090
00:58:49.735 --> 00:58:51.988
Hey, I don't remember
coming this way.

1091
00:58:52.821 --> 00:58:55.074
Must be one of
Scowler's shortcuts.

1092
00:58:56.408 --> 00:58:57.785
Hmm.

1093
00:59:04.458 --> 00:59:07.086
Come on, people, try
to keep up here.

1094
00:59:07.753 --> 00:59:10.302
Whoa! I heard laughing,
who's laughing?

1095
00:59:10.630 --> 00:59:11.677
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1096
00:59:48.668 --> 00:59:49.728
<font color="#808080">(GROANS)</font>

1097
00:59:49.753 --> 00:59:53.648
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: I can't believe we're on a
frozen lake in the middle of spring.

1098
00:59:53.673 --> 00:59:54.674
<font color="#808080">(ICE CRACKING)</font>

1099
00:59:56.218 --> 00:59:59.688
Wait a minute. We're on a frozen
lake in the middle of spring?

1100
00:59:59.846 --> 01:00:01.018
Juniper!

1101
01:00:01.181 --> 01:00:02.774
Tell Scowler it's not safe!

1102
01:00:02.933 --> 01:00:05.732
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: He won't listen to me.
He won't listen to anybody.

1103
01:00:06.269 --> 01:00:07.612
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1104
01:00:12.109 --> 01:00:15.613
Juniper, you have to believe me,
we need to get off this ice!

1105
01:00:15.779 --> 01:00:20.250
But Scowler's the herd leader. We
have to follow him, it's the rule.

1106
01:00:20.700 --> 01:00:21.792
Oh, no!

1107
01:00:27.040 --> 01:00:29.384
I told you guys to
pick up the pace!

1108
01:00:29.543 --> 01:00:31.921
Come on! No retreating!

1109
01:00:33.170 --> 01:00:34.731
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>While Scowler
blundered forward...</i>

1110
01:00:34.756 --> 01:00:37.635
<i>Patchi knew he had to move
the herd off the ice.</i>

1111
01:00:37.801 --> 01:00:40.224
Everybody, back to shore!

1112
01:00:40.929 --> 01:00:42.772
Turn back, everyone.

1113
01:00:44.474 --> 01:00:48.229
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: You guys, it's not safe!
We need to turn back!

1114
01:00:51.148 --> 01:00:54.743
Come on, little guy, I got you.
That's it.

1115
01:00:54.901 --> 01:00:57.780
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Let's go!
Everybody follow me!

1116
01:01:00.615 --> 01:01:02.743
Everyone off the ice!

1117
01:01:04.411 --> 01:01:05.833
On to shore, everybody!

1118
01:01:06.246 --> 01:01:08.089
Just push in!

1119
01:01:13.628 --> 01:01:16.598
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Patchi! What now?!
There's too many of us!

1120
01:01:16.840 --> 01:01:19.218
Okay. Think! Um...

1121
01:01:19.509 --> 01:01:22.934
Knock down the tree and feast
on the leafy Greens up top.

1122
01:01:23.096 --> 01:01:24.769
That's it! Follow me!

1123
01:01:24.931 --> 01:01:26.308
This way!

1124
01:01:32.439 --> 01:01:33.861
<font color="#808080">(BANGING)</font>

1125
01:01:37.777 --> 01:01:39.120
Keep moving!

1126
01:01:39.279 --> 01:01:41.452
Push down the trees!
Make a path!

1127
01:01:43.283 --> 01:01:45.377
Take that, random tree!

1128
01:01:45.994 --> 01:01:47.429
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Whoo-hoo!

1129
01:01:47.454 --> 01:01:49.627
Good job, Patchi!

1130
01:01:51.958 --> 01:01:53.768
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1131
01:01:53.793 --> 01:01:56.012
Hey! He's taking my herd!

1132
01:01:56.171 --> 01:01:57.798
Oh, so cold!

1133
01:01:58.131 --> 01:02:02.136
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Patchi's quick thinking had
saved the herd from</i> a <i>frigid fate...</i>

1134
01:02:02.302 --> 01:02:04.851
<i>but not everyone was
grateful for his heroics.</i>

1135
01:02:05.013 --> 01:02:06.014
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Come on!

1136
01:02:06.181 --> 01:02:07.728
Hey, who do you think
you are, huh?!

1137
01:02:07.891 --> 01:02:10.565
Boy, looks like Scowler's
pretty mad, huh?

1138
01:02:10.727 --> 01:02:12.650
We better just keep moving.

1139
01:02:18.985 --> 01:02:20.578
Hey, Patchi!

1140
01:02:21.363 --> 01:02:24.583
Look at me! You can't
just take my herd!

1141
01:02:24.741 --> 01:02:26.743
That's not the way
things are done!

1142
01:02:26.868 --> 01:02:28.836
There's rules, you know!
Come here!

1143
01:02:29.079 --> 01:02:32.925
I didn't take them, all right, Scowler?
I had to get them off the ice.

1144
01:02:33.083 --> 01:02:34.551
You're welcome to join us!

1145
01:02:34.709 --> 01:02:36.256
Oh, don't worry, Patchi...

1146
01:02:36.419 --> 01:02:38.922
I will find you
wherever you go!

1147
01:02:39.798 --> 01:02:41.391
And then we'll see what's up!

1148
01:02:41.549 --> 01:02:43.597
Whatever you say, Scowler.

1149
01:02:50.976 --> 01:02:54.731
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>The shadows grew long as the
sun kissed the Western horizon...</i>

1150
01:02:54.896 --> 01:02:58.400
<i>casting a ghostly glow over
our fearless protagonist...</i>

1151
01:02:58.566 --> 01:03:00.364
<i>and also on Patchi.</i>

1152
01:03:00.944 --> 01:03:03.072
I hope Scowler wasn't
serious back there.

1153
01:03:03.238 --> 01:03:06.287
He's probably just letting off
steam. He'll get over it.

1154
01:03:06.449 --> 01:03:07.792
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Surprise! Ha ha!

1155
01:03:07.951 --> 01:03:10.045
So glad you're here,
'cause it's time

1156
01:03:10.203 --> 01:03:12.251
to get down to business, Patchi!

1157
01:03:12.414 --> 01:03:14.291
Okay. He's not over it.

1158
01:03:23.008 --> 01:03:25.010
Just ignore him.
Let's keep going.

1159
01:03:25.176 --> 01:03:27.099
You're right, come on.

1160
01:03:27.345 --> 01:03:30.865
Hey, Patchi, where you off
to in such a hurry, huh?

1161
01:03:30.890 --> 01:03:32.563
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1162
01:03:34.519 --> 01:03:37.773
Patchi, don't engage him,
don't take the bait.

1163
01:03:38.648 --> 01:03:39.991
What do you want, Scowler?

1164
01:03:40.483 --> 01:03:42.736
You stole my herd,
you stole my girl

1165
01:03:42.902 --> 01:03:45.200
and now you're
gonna pay for it.

1166
01:03:45.363 --> 01:03:46.660
You crossed the line.

1167
01:03:47.615 --> 01:03:51.495
You crossed the line when you almost
got everyone killed back there.

1168
01:03:51.661 --> 01:03:55.056
Tough talk for a little guy.
Let's see if you can back it up.

1169
01:03:55.081 --> 01:03:56.378
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1170
01:03:59.336 --> 01:04:03.011
You can have the herd, but
you're not taking Juniper.

1171
01:04:03.173 --> 01:04:06.302
You don't have to do this, Patchi,
you don't have to fight him.

1172
01:04:12.223 --> 01:04:13.896
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

1173
01:04:26.446 --> 01:04:27.447
<font color="#808080">(CHIRPS)</font>

1174
01:04:49.969 --> 01:04:51.937
Last chance to walk away!

1175
01:04:52.097 --> 01:04:53.519
What's it gonna be?

1176
01:04:53.681 --> 01:04:56.230
This ends here!

1177
01:05:14.661 --> 01:05:15.662
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Give up!

1178
01:05:15.829 --> 01:05:17.251
Yeah, come on!

1179
01:05:25.547 --> 01:05:27.845
Oh, you're tougher
than I thought.

1180
01:05:59.998 --> 01:06:01.716
You want some more, Patch?

1181
01:06:02.041 --> 01:06:03.042
That's what I thought.

1182
01:06:03.418 --> 01:06:06.638
And by the way, you're
out of the herd.

1183
01:06:08.965 --> 01:06:10.308
Move out!

1184
01:06:18.016 --> 01:06:19.609
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Patchi, are
you all right?!

1185
01:06:20.477 --> 01:06:21.774
Patchi?

1186
01:06:21.936 --> 01:06:25.486
Okay, hang in there, I'm gonna help you.
<font color="#808080">(GROWLING)</font>

1187
01:06:26.983 --> 01:06:31.079
What are you doing, Juniper? I
said move out. You know the rules.

1188
01:06:31.946 --> 01:06:35.120
You can't just leave him like
that, he's your brother.

1189
01:06:35.283 --> 01:06:36.830
I don't have a brother.

1190
01:06:36.993 --> 01:06:39.087
Now get back to the herd!

1191
01:06:41.706 --> 01:06:44.334
Juniper, don't go.

1192
01:06:46.044 --> 01:06:48.217
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Well, this is the way
it goes for some of us.</i>

1193
01:06:48.379 --> 01:06:50.882
<i>We try our best, we
fight the good fight...</i>

1194
01:06:51.049 --> 01:06:55.930
<i>and yet we cannot succeed
against the greater forces.</i>

1195
01:06:57.055 --> 01:06:59.353
<i>Aye, poor Patchi.
Lying helpless</i>

1196
01:06:59.474 --> 01:07:01.818
<i>with the weight of the
world on his shoulders.</i>

1197
01:07:01.976 --> 01:07:05.105
<i>What could bring him back
from the brink of despair?</i>

1198
01:07:05.271 --> 01:07:07.945
<i>Well, that's what
friends are for.</i>

1199
01:07:10.360 --> 01:07:11.577
Patchi! <font color="#808080">(TAPPING)</font>

1200
01:07:12.403 --> 01:07:13.505
Patchi?

1201
01:07:13.530 --> 01:07:16.033
Patchi, come on, you've
got to get up, buddy.

1202
01:07:16.199 --> 01:07:18.076
Come on, Patchi, please.
Talk to me.

1203
01:07:18.243 --> 01:07:20.211
What is the problem?
Are you hurt?

1204
01:07:20.662 --> 01:07:22.039
How about now?

1205
01:07:22.789 --> 01:07:26.760
And what about this? Does
that hurt? A little bit?

1206
01:07:28.711 --> 01:07:30.964
Uh-oh. Scavengers!

1207
01:07:32.632 --> 01:07:34.009
Hey! Get out of here!

1208
01:07:34.467 --> 01:07:36.686
Return to your home, nothing
to see here! Go away!

1209
01:07:36.844 --> 01:07:38.642
Shoo, shoo!

1210
01:07:38.805 --> 01:07:40.398
Patchi, get up!

1211
01:07:40.557 --> 01:07:41.558
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: No.

1212
01:07:41.724 --> 01:07:43.317
This is where I belong.

1213
01:07:43.476 --> 01:07:48.403
Aw, Alex, what an idiot I was,
trying to be the big man...

1214
01:07:48.565 --> 01:07:51.910
thinking I could beat Scowler
and be with Juniper.

1215
01:07:52.068 --> 01:07:56.164
No, my friend, you are confusing
ambition with destiny!

1216
01:07:56.322 --> 01:07:57.722
Now, I told you when
you were little

1217
01:07:57.824 --> 01:07:59.167
that you were going
to be a hero!

1218
01:07:59.325 --> 01:08:01.327
And an Alexornis never lies!

1219
01:08:01.494 --> 01:08:04.247
Patchi, please, these guys
aren't fooling around, okay?

1220
01:08:04.414 --> 01:08:05.961
They're gonna have
a dinner party

1221
01:08:05.964 --> 01:08:07.684
and I'm telling you,
you're the main course!

1222
01:08:07.709 --> 01:08:08.810
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Good.

1223
01:08:08.835 --> 01:08:11.839
Shame on you. Imagine what your
father, Bulldust, would say to that.

1224
01:08:12.005 --> 01:08:13.006
I don't care.

1225
01:08:13.172 --> 01:08:14.173
I have no reason to...

1226
01:08:14.382 --> 01:08:15.884
Ouch! Okay, that hurt.

1227
01:08:16.342 --> 01:08:18.344
Uh-oh. More customers.

1228
01:08:19.387 --> 01:08:20.764
Come on, move it, big guy!

1229
01:08:20.930 --> 01:08:23.024
Alex, would you just go away?

1230
01:08:23.182 --> 01:08:25.059
I don't want you to see this.

1231
01:08:25.226 --> 01:08:27.024
No, Patchi! Don't
let this happen!

1232
01:08:27.186 --> 01:08:29.735
Come on! Just get
it over with.

1233
01:08:29.897 --> 01:08:31.695
Put me out of my misery.

1234
01:08:34.360 --> 01:08:35.361
Ow!

1235
01:08:35.528 --> 01:08:36.529
Patchi...

1236
01:08:37.030 --> 01:08:38.122
listen to me.

1237
01:08:38.740 --> 01:08:40.617
Do not die in vain.

1238
01:08:40.867 --> 01:08:45.293
If you're going to die, die for
something like your father did.

1239
01:08:45.455 --> 01:08:47.378
He died for you.

1240
01:08:47.540 --> 01:08:50.134
<i>But you have someone
to live for.</i>

1241
01:08:50.293 --> 01:08:51.419
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: <i>Juniper.</i>

1242
01:08:54.881 --> 01:08:55.882
Juniper!

1243
01:08:56.132 --> 01:08:57.133
Getup!

1244
01:08:57.383 --> 01:08:58.600
<font color="#808080">(GROANING)</font>

1245
01:09:00.720 --> 01:09:03.394
Get up! Get up, Patchi!

1246
01:09:03.556 --> 01:09:04.728
Get it off me!

1247
01:09:07.060 --> 01:09:09.120
You are not a piece of meat.

1248
01:09:09.145 --> 01:09:11.318
I am not a piece of meat!

1249
01:09:11.731 --> 01:09:13.404
Get outta here!

1250
01:09:14.108 --> 01:09:15.826
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

1251
01:09:22.158 --> 01:09:23.785
I'm not afraid of you!

1252
01:09:24.077 --> 01:09:26.421
I'm not afraid of anyone!

1253
01:09:28.414 --> 01:09:31.759
Wow, that was something! What
did you eat for breakfast?

1254
01:09:31.918 --> 01:09:34.592
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: I ate a bush,
if you must know.

1255
01:09:39.801 --> 01:09:42.099
I'm back! Yes!

1256
01:09:43.846 --> 01:09:47.476
Look out! Pachyrhinosaur,
on the move!

1257
01:09:48.810 --> 01:09:51.029
Yes, Patchi, lumber!

1258
01:09:51.312 --> 01:09:53.531
Lumber like the wind!

1259
01:09:55.983 --> 01:09:58.281
What are you looking at?
Scram, punks!

1260
01:09:59.987 --> 01:10:02.536
Gotta get back,
gotta get back.

1261
01:10:03.700 --> 01:10:07.204
Out of my way, skinny-neck pecky things!
<font color="#808080">(PANTING)</font>

1262
01:10:08.913 --> 01:10:09.914
<font color="#808080">(SCREECHING)</font>

1263
01:10:10.289 --> 01:10:12.291
Yeah, right back at you!

1264
01:10:12.792 --> 01:10:15.261
Gotta get back,
gotta get back.

1265
01:10:22.135 --> 01:10:26.265
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>What Patchi lacked in size,
he made up for in courage.</i>

1266
01:10:26.431 --> 01:10:28.658
<i>For nothing would stop him.</i>

1267
01:10:28.683 --> 01:10:30.151
<i>Not this time.</i>

1268
01:10:34.105 --> 01:10:35.106
I made it.

1269
01:10:35.481 --> 01:10:36.949
I made it.

1270
01:10:40.486 --> 01:10:41.533
Juniper!

1271
01:10:42.655 --> 01:10:44.465
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>He tracked
along the fringes,</i>

1272
01:10:44.490 --> 01:10:47.334
<i>looking for the one who
was once lost to him...</i>

1273
01:10:47.493 --> 01:10:50.838
<i>but who now had given him
his new sense of purpose.</i>

1274
01:10:50.997 --> 01:10:53.716
Hey, everybody! Has
anyone seen Juniper?

1275
01:10:54.041 --> 01:10:55.839
Anyone? Anyone.

1276
01:10:56.002 --> 01:10:57.800
Just a quick yes or no.

1277
01:10:58.379 --> 01:10:59.380
There she is!

1278
01:11:00.006 --> 01:11:01.007
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1279
01:11:01.632 --> 01:11:02.633
Juniper!

1280
01:11:03.468 --> 01:11:05.015
Juniper! Excuse me!

1281
01:11:05.178 --> 01:11:07.101
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Patchi's hardships
were swept away</i>

1282
01:11:07.221 --> 01:11:09.144
<i>by the vision of
his true love.</i>

1283
01:11:09.307 --> 01:11:13.528
<i>His heart Sang and his spirit
soared, and at that moment...</i>

1284
01:11:13.686 --> 01:11:15.955
<i>he would have walked through
a thousand dinosaur butts...</i>

1285
01:11:15.980 --> 01:11:20.326
<i>or even a million, if only to
get to his beloved Juniper.</i>

1286
01:11:22.570 --> 01:11:24.297
Patchi, you're okay!

1287
01:11:24.322 --> 01:11:26.666
I was afraid I was never
going to see you again.

1288
01:11:26.824 --> 01:11:28.201
Don't worry, you'll be
seeing plenty more of me,

1289
01:11:28.326 --> 01:11:30.374
because there's something
I want to tell you.

1290
01:11:30.536 --> 01:11:32.538
- Really?
- I'm just gonna say it.

1291
01:11:32.705 --> 01:11:33.877
Go on.

1292
01:11:34.040 --> 01:11:35.349
Because this is
the right moment.

1293
01:11:35.374 --> 01:11:37.143
- Say it!
- Juniper...

1294
01:11:37.168 --> 01:11:38.561
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

1295
01:11:38.586 --> 01:11:39.645
Huh?

1296
01:11:39.670 --> 01:11:41.764
What is it? Wait,
what's going on?

1297
01:11:41.923 --> 01:11:43.049
What's all the panic?

1298
01:11:43.216 --> 01:11:45.184
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Patchi would soon
realize that the herd</i>

1299
01:11:45.301 --> 01:11:47.269
<i>had entered an all-too-familiar
mountain pass.</i>

1300
01:11:47.553 --> 01:11:50.773
Wait, I know this place.
Ambush Alley.

1301
01:11:51.265 --> 01:11:54.610
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Ambush alley, Dead Man's
Canyon, Scowler's Folly.</i>

1302
01:11:54.769 --> 01:11:57.249
<i>That's a new name, by the way.
And you'll know why in a minute.</i>

1303
01:11:57.396 --> 01:12:00.275
Patchi, the Gorges! We've
gotta get out of here, now!

1304
01:12:00.566 --> 01:12:02.068
<font color="#808080">(GRUNTING)</font>
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Scowler?

1305
01:12:04.237 --> 01:12:05.454
Scowler!

1306
01:12:08.282 --> 01:12:11.877
Patchi, don't just stand there!
Get out of here! Run!

1307
01:12:12.578 --> 01:12:15.548
But you're my brother! We
have to stick together!

1308
01:12:17.208 --> 01:12:18.601
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1309
01:12:18.626 --> 01:12:21.095
I meant, run away!

1310
01:12:21.254 --> 01:12:22.597
I know what you meant.

1311
01:12:22.755 --> 01:12:24.473
Go on! Don't worry,
I'm wearing them out!

1312
01:12:24.924 --> 01:12:26.267
I'm not going anywhere!

1313
01:12:26.425 --> 01:12:27.768
Patchi, save the herd!

1314
01:12:27.927 --> 01:12:29.975
Lead them to safety!

1315
01:12:30.388 --> 01:12:34.393
You don't owe me anything,
little bro! Don't be a hero!

1316
01:12:35.268 --> 01:12:37.942
What do I do? What do I do?

1317
01:12:38.980 --> 01:12:40.448
Hang on, you guys!

1318
01:12:40.606 --> 01:12:43.780
I'm going to give you some air
support! Everybody look to the skies!

1319
01:12:43.943 --> 01:12:45.991
Help is on the way!

1320
01:12:46.612 --> 01:12:47.955
Hold on. Bug break.

1321
01:12:48.114 --> 01:12:50.833
An army marches on it's
stomach, you know.

1322
01:12:51.242 --> 01:12:53.290
You know I'm right, Patchi.

1323
01:12:53.452 --> 01:12:55.250
I'm already a goner.

1324
01:12:55.413 --> 01:12:56.835
Take the herd away from here!

1325
01:12:58.249 --> 01:12:59.671
Go while you still can!

1326
01:13:09.468 --> 01:13:10.811
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Patchi.</i>

1327
01:13:11.429 --> 01:13:13.022
<i>Do not die in vain.</i>

1328
01:13:14.181 --> 01:13:16.183
<i>If you are going to die,</i>

1329
01:13:16.851 --> 01:13:19.604
<i>die for something
like your father did.</i>

1330
01:13:20.479 --> 01:13:22.197
<i>He died for you.</i>

1331
01:13:30.823 --> 01:13:32.291
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1332
01:13:34.702 --> 01:13:37.831
That's right, I'm talking
to you, tiny arms.

1333
01:13:39.832 --> 01:13:42.051
Everyone, follow me!

1334
01:13:42.460 --> 01:13:43.507
Come on!

1335
01:13:51.719 --> 01:13:52.845
<font color="#808080">(GROANING)</font>

1336
01:13:54.680 --> 01:13:57.024
You messed with the
wrong herd, lizard boy!

1337
01:13:57.141 --> 01:13:59.485
You're about to get served!

1338
01:14:01.520 --> 01:14:02.942
Told you!

1339
01:14:25.211 --> 01:14:27.464
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Both sides
battled ferociously...</i>

1340
01:14:27.630 --> 01:14:31.555
<i>but the Pachyrhinosaurs had one
thing the Gorgosaurs did not:</i>

1341
01:14:31.717 --> 01:14:33.560
<i>A former runt with a
hole in his head...</i>

1342
01:14:34.053 --> 01:14:35.976
<i>and a lion in his heart.</i>

1343
01:14:39.058 --> 01:14:41.060
<i>But even the greatest
of heroes...</i>

1344
01:14:41.227 --> 01:14:44.705
<i>can sometimes benefit
from a lucky break.</i>

1345
01:14:44.730 --> 01:14:46.528
<font color="#808080">(SNAPS)</font>
<font color="#808080">(SCREECHING)</font>

1346
01:14:47.066 --> 01:14:50.536
That one's for my brother!
And that one's for my dad!

1347
01:14:50.736 --> 01:14:51.908
And this one...

1348
01:15:01.080 --> 01:15:03.208
That's so you'll remember me!

1349
01:15:09.755 --> 01:15:13.100
That's right, you heard me.
Get out of here!

1350
01:15:16.762 --> 01:15:20.642
Name's Patchi! And I'll
see you next winter!

1351
01:15:20.808 --> 01:15:22.105
<font color="#808080">(ROARING)</font>

1352
01:15:33.946 --> 01:15:37.041
I don't believe it.
Patchi did it!

1353
01:15:45.332 --> 01:15:48.211
I was distracted. What happened?
Did we win'?

1354
01:15:48.377 --> 01:15:50.379
What happened? Payback.

1355
01:15:50.629 --> 01:15:52.506
That's what happened.

1356
01:15:54.550 --> 01:15:56.973
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>I'm telling you, you
can't make this stuff up.</i>

1357
01:15:57.136 --> 01:15:59.138
<i>After everything
he'd been through,</i>

1358
01:15:59.305 --> 01:16:01.307
<i>Patchi's moment had
finally arrived.</i>

1359
01:16:01.474 --> 01:16:04.353
<i>He was the undisputed
leader of the herd...</i>

1360
01:16:04.518 --> 01:16:06.896
<i>and nobody was
prouder than me.</i>

1361
01:16:07.855 --> 01:16:09.107
You hurt, Scowler?

1362
01:16:09.273 --> 01:16:10.866
I'm okay. Thanks.

1363
01:16:11.067 --> 01:16:14.947
You know, Patch, you didn't
have to do that after...

1364
01:16:15.112 --> 01:16:17.035
you know, what I did to you.

1365
01:16:17.198 --> 01:16:18.799
So I just wanted to say...
<font color="#808080">(ROARS LOUDLY)</font>

1366
01:16:21.327 --> 01:16:22.954
I deserve that.

1367
01:16:23.579 --> 01:16:26.378
Guess this means you're the
leader of the herd now.

1368
01:16:26.540 --> 01:16:28.542
So, you might as well
go ahead and say it.

1369
01:16:28.709 --> 01:16:29.961
Really? Okay.

1370
01:16:30.127 --> 01:16:32.004
Well, let's move 'em out!

1371
01:16:32.588 --> 01:16:33.589
<font color="#804040">SCOWLER</font>: Sounds good.

1372
01:16:33.756 --> 01:16:35.554
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Yeah, that
felt pretty good.

1373
01:16:36.175 --> 01:16:38.769
Hey, Patchi, you were
pretty great out there.

1374
01:16:38.928 --> 01:16:42.398
Yeah, you too. Remind me
never to headbutt with you.

1375
01:16:42.598 --> 01:16:45.147
Juniper, listen, it's time
to talk about the future.

1376
01:16:45.309 --> 01:16:47.687
You mean the Cenozoic Era?

1377
01:16:47.853 --> 01:16:51.198
No, I mean the Patchi
and Juniper Era.

1378
01:16:51.357 --> 01:16:54.327
Oh, I think I'm gonna
like the future.

1379
01:17:05.454 --> 01:17:07.181
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>With the
herd at his heels,</i>

1380
01:17:07.206 --> 01:17:10.130
<i>Patchi walked across the
grasslands of Alaska...</i>

1381
01:17:10.292 --> 01:17:11.714
<i>and into the future.</i>

1382
01:17:13.921 --> 01:17:17.425
<i>Which, as always, was
full of surprises.</i>

1383
01:17:22.972 --> 01:17:24.315
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: Excuse me?!

1384
01:17:25.266 --> 01:17:26.939
Hi, there. Can I help
you find something?

1385
01:17:27.810 --> 01:17:29.153
No'? You sure?

1386
01:17:29.311 --> 01:17:31.564
Okay, then get out!
<font color="#808080">(SHRIEKS)</font>

1387
01:17:32.982 --> 01:17:35.861
Go back to Turkey
town and stay out!

1388
01:17:36.026 --> 01:17:39.030
Patchi, are you messing
with the Troodons again?

1389
01:17:39.196 --> 01:17:41.164
I thought I asked you
to watch the eggs.

1390
01:17:41.574 --> 01:17:45.795
I am watching them, but they
keep not doing anything.

1391
01:17:45.953 --> 01:17:49.628
I told you, it takes time.
You have to be patient.

1392
01:17:49.790 --> 01:17:52.339
<font color="#804040">PATCHI</font>: I know, but we're
talking about our whole future.

1393
01:17:52.501 --> 01:17:55.425
Why does the future always
take so long to get here?

1394
01:17:56.714 --> 01:17:59.092
<font color="#804040">JUNIPER</font>: Shh! You hear that?

1395
01:18:00.759 --> 01:18:02.887
It's time, Patchi. This is it!

1396
01:18:03.053 --> 01:18:04.805
I don't believe it.

1397
01:18:07.975 --> 01:18:10.411
Wow, look at that!

1398
01:18:10.436 --> 01:18:12.564
Oh, he's beautiful.

1399
01:18:12.771 --> 01:18:14.239
He looks just
like his old man.

1400
01:18:14.648 --> 01:18:17.902
Well, if he's anything like
you, we'll have our hands full.

1401
01:18:18.068 --> 01:18:20.162
Well, look what we have here.

1402
01:18:20.321 --> 01:18:23.996
Allow me to congratulate you
on this happiest of occasions.

1403
01:18:24.158 --> 01:18:27.628
As far as names go,
may I suggest Alex?

1404
01:18:27.786 --> 01:18:30.630
It means, "Ridiculously
handsome bird."

1405
01:18:30.956 --> 01:18:34.256
And <i>as</i> for you, baby
Alex, how about a kiss?

1406
01:18:34.418 --> 01:18:35.965
Okay, bye-bye.

1407
01:18:37.630 --> 01:18:39.724
♪ <i> Live like a warrior</i> ♪

1408
01:18:40.674 --> 01:18:43.277
♪ <i> Today, today, ♪
♪ live like you wanna</i> ♪

1409
01:18:43.302 --> 01:18:46.739
♪ <i> Let yesterday burn ♪
♪ and throw it in a fire</i> ♪

1410
01:18:46.764 --> 01:18:49.062
♪ <i> In a fire In a fire</i> ♪

1411
01:18:49.475 --> 01:18:53.321
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Patchi's story may have faded
into the mosaic of history...</i>

1412
01:18:54.146 --> 01:18:56.615
but <i>evidence of the day
that a Gorgosaur's mouth...</i>

1413
01:18:56.774 --> 01:19:00.745
<i>ran into a Pachyrhinosaur's
head still exists.</i>

1414
01:19:01.320 --> 01:19:04.073
<i>And what happened after that,
well, that's hard to say.</i>

1415
01:19:05.282 --> 01:19:07.250
<i>It's a question
that has intrigued</i>

1416
01:19:07.368 --> 01:19:09.336
<i>dinosaur lovers
for generations.</i>

1417
01:19:10.663 --> 01:19:15.419
<i>I'll only say that sometimes, you
have to dig for the answers.</i>

1418
01:19:15.918 --> 01:19:17.170
A Gorgosaur's?

1419
01:19:17.294 --> 01:19:18.511
Looks to be.

1420
01:19:18.671 --> 01:19:20.173
Uncle Zack?

1421
01:19:21.215 --> 01:19:22.387
Hey, Ricky.

1422
01:19:23.384 --> 01:19:25.261
Come see what we found.

1423
01:19:32.601 --> 01:19:33.602
Uncle Zack...

1424
01:19:34.103 --> 01:19:35.320
look, the tooth!

1425
01:19:35.479 --> 01:19:37.106
Ricky, did you bring it?

1426
01:19:37.606 --> 01:19:38.732
Here it is.

1427
01:19:40.776 --> 01:19:42.278
- <font color="#804040">RICKY</font>: Cool!
- <font color="#804040">UNCLE ZACK</font>: Wow!

1428
01:19:42.444 --> 01:19:43.445
That's it, it fits!

1429
01:19:43.612 --> 01:19:45.910
I knew it'd be worth coming back!
<font color="#808080">(SQUAWKING)</font>

1430
01:19:46.323 --> 01:19:49.042
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Kid, What
did I tell you?</i>

1431
01:19:49.201 --> 01:19:51.829
<i>Every fossil tells a story!</i>

1432
01:19:51.996 --> 01:19:54.465
<i>Hey, come and see me
in a museum sometime.</i>

1433
01:19:54.623 --> 01:19:57.172
<i>I got my own diorama
and a tiki bar!</i>

1434
01:19:58.252 --> 01:20:00.880
<i>As for the rest of you,
this is the end of my tail.</i>

1435
01:20:01.046 --> 01:20:04.141
<i>No, literally, you see it? No,
really, honestly, it's the end.</i>

1436
01:20:04.300 --> 01:20:06.944
<i>That's it. We're done.
Fade to black.</i>

1437
01:20:06.969 --> 01:20:08.312
<font color="#808080">(GROWLING)</font>

1438
01:20:10.806 --> 01:20:12.149
<font color="#808080">(ROARS)</font>

1439
01:20:12.817 --> 01:20:14.618
<font color="#804040">ALEX</font>: <i>Oops, forgot about that part.
<font color="#808080">(CHUCKLES)</font></i>

1440
01:20:14.643 --> 01:20:15.644
<i>Gotcha!</i>

